2026-11-25 22:32:25.811 | DEBUG    | agent.middlewares.summarization.memory_review:_invoke_memory_review:281 - memory review res is content='I have enough material for the report. Producing it now.\n\n## Recon Report — actionlint @ `0bdc95715fa5`\n\n### 1. `config.go` (161 lines) — Config struct, YAML, path overrides, validation style\n\n| Item | Location | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `IgnorePatterns []*regexp.Regexp` + `Match(*Error) bool` | `config.go:15-27` | Filters by `err.Message` regexp |\n| `PathConfig` (per-glob override) | `config.go:~30-45` | Has `Ignore IgnorePatterns`; unmarshalled via custom `UnmarshalYAML` (error style: `"ignore" must be a sequence node`, `invalid regular expression %q in "ignore"`) |\n| `Config` struct | `config.go:~48-72` | Fields: `SelfHostedRunner struct{ Labels []string }`, `ConfigVariables []string`, `Paths map[string]PathConfig` |\n| `(*Config).PathConfigs(path string) []PathConfig` | `config.go:74-87` | Iterates `c.Paths`, `doublestar.Match(pat, path)`; returns matching `PathConfig`s |\n| `ParseConfig(b []byte) (*Config, error)` | `config.go:89-103` | `yaml.Unmarshal` (go.yaml.in/yaml/v4), newlines flattened to spaces; then validates each `paths` key with `doublestar.ValidatePattern` → `fmt.Errorf("invalid glob pattern %q in \\"paths\\"", pat)` |\n| `ReadConfigFile(path)` | `config.go:105-116` | Wraps errors: `could not read config file %q: %w`, `could not parse config file %q: %w` |\n| `loadRepoConfig` | `config.go:118-~140` | Reads `.github/actionlint.yaml` / `.yml` from project root |\n| `writeDefaultConfigFile` | `config.go:~142-161` | Emits commented template; the `paths:` block is at `config.go:153-156` — **this is where a new config key\'s commented example belongs** |\n\n**Validation/error style:** plain `fmt.Errorf` with lowercase message, `%q` for user values, no custom error types. Validation happens inside `ParseConfig` after unmarshal (see the glob-pattern loop at `config.go:97-101`). A new config section should follow the same pattern: unmarshal into a struct field, then validate in `ParseConfig` and return `fmt.Errorf(...)`.\n\n### 2. `rule.go` / `linter.go` — rule declaration, registration, config threading, errors\n\n- `RuleBase` (`rule.go:10-16`): `name, desc, errs []*Error, dbg io.Writer, config *Config`.\n- `NewRuleBase(name, desc)` (`rule.go:20-25`).\n- `RuleBase.Errorf(pos, format, args...)` / `Error(pos, msg)` / `Debug(...)` — append to `r.errs`; `Errs()` returns them (`rule.go:27-~90`).\n- `SetConfig(cfg *Config)` / `Config() *Config` (`rule.go:~88-97`); `Config()` returns `nil` when unset.\n- `Rule` interface (`rule.go:100-108`): `Pass`, `Errs()`, `Name()`, `Description()`, `EnableDebug(io.Writer)`, `SetConfig(*Config)`, `Config() *Config`.\n- **Registration**: `linter.go:557-573` — the `rules := []Rule{...}` literal inside `LintFile`/`check` (function starting ~`linter.go:519`). New rules are appended here; external rules via `l.shellcheck`/`l.pyflakes` blocks (`linter.go:574-593`) and the `OnRulesCreated` hook (`linter.go:594-596`).\n- **Config threading**: `linter.go:534-545` picks `l.defaultConfig` (from `-config-file`) else `project.Config()`; `linter.go:608-612` calls `r.SetConfig(cfg)` on every rule **only when cfg != nil**. So a rule must handle `rule.config == nil` (see `rule_runner_label.go:328-333`, `rule_expression.go:770-773`).\n- **Error production**: `rule.Errorf(pos, ...)`; `Error` struct in `error.go` with `Message`, `Filepath`, `Line`, `Column`, `Kind`; `errorAt`/`errorfAt` helpers at `error.go:~50-64`. Errors are collected at `linter.go:619-623`, filtered at `linter.go:632` via `l.filterErrors(all, cfg.PathConfigs(path))` (`linter.go:649-673`).\n\n### 3. CLI — `cmd/actionlint/main.go` and `command.go`\n\n- `cmd/actionlint/main.go` is a 16-line shim: builds `actionlint.Command{Stdin, Stdout, Stderr}` and calls `cmd.Main(os.Args)`.\n- **All flags live in `command.go`**: `ignorePatternFlags` type at `command.go:113-121`; `flags := flag.NewFlagSet(...)` at `command.go:134`; flags registered at `command.go:136-~150` (`-ignore`, `-shellcheck`, `-pyflakes`, `-config-file`, `-format`, `-init-config`, `-color`, `-oneline`, `-verbose`, `-debug`, `-stdin-filename`, `-version`, …). They map into `LinterOptions` (`linter.go:40-95`) and then `NewLinter` (`linter.go:118-200`).\n- **Insertion point for a new flag**: add `flags.BoolVar(&opts.X, "x", false, "...")` next to the existing ones in `command.go:~136-150`, add the field to `LinterOptions` (`linter.go:~60-94`), copy it into the `Linter` struct (`linter.go:98-112`) and the positional literal in `NewLinter` (`linter.go:182-196`), then use it in `check` (`linter.go:519+`).\n\n### 4. Config-aware rule templates\n\n- **`rule_runner_label.go`** — best template: `getKnownLabels()` at `rule_runner_label.go:328-333` reads `rule.config.SelfHostedRunner.Labels` with a nil guard. Test pattern: `rule_runner_label_test.go:322-327` builds `cfg := Config{}`, sets fields, `rule.SetConfig(&cfg)`, then calls `rule.VisitJobPre(node)` directly.\n- **`rule_expression.go:769-773`** — reads `rule.config.ConfigVariables` with nil guard.\n- **`rule_permissions.go`** — simplest rule skeleton (no config): struct embedding `RuleBase` (`:26-28`), `NewRulePermissions()` (`:31-38`), `VisitJobPre`/`VisitWorkflowPre` (`:41-50`), `checkPermissions` (`:52+`) using `rule.Errorf(pos, ...)`.\n- **`rule_workflow_call.go`** — the reusable-workflow rule: `VisitJobPre` (`:45-77`) reads `n.WorkflowCall.Uses`, skips `nil`/empty/`ContainsExpression()`, distinguishes local (`./…`) vs repo (`owner/repo/path@ref`) formats via `isWorkflowCallUsesLocalFormat` / `isWorkflowCallUsesRepoFormat`, and emits `rule.Errorf(u.Pos, ...)`.\n\n### 5. Distinguishing reusable-workflow calls from step actions\n\n- **Step action**: `Step.Exec` is `*ExecAction` with `Uses *String` — see `rule_action.go:317-344` (`VisitStep`), which skips when `!ok || e.Uses == nil` or `e.Uses.ContainsExpression()`, then branches on `./` (local), `docker://`, else `{owner}/{repo}@{ref}` parsing in `checkRepoAction` (`rule_action.go:347-392`).\n- **Reusable workflow call**: `Job.WorkflowCall *WorkflowCall` (`ast.go:923-925`), `WorkflowCall.Uses *String` (`ast.go:846-860`). `Job` struct starts at `ast.go:876`. `WorkflowCallEvent` at `ast.go:309`; `Workflow.FindWorkflowCallEvent()` at `ast.go:959-967`.\n- So: `steps[].uses` → `VisitStep` + `*ExecAction`; `jobs.<id>.uses` → `VisitJobPre` + `n.WorkflowCall != nil` + `n.WorkflowCall.Uses`.\n\n### 6. Known-actions data\n\n- `popular_actions.go` — `PopularActions map[string]*ActionMetadata` (keyed by full `owner/repo@ref` spec) and `OutdatedPopularActionSpecs`. Used at `rule_action.go:375-383`. `ActionMetadata` is in `action_metadata.go` (fields include `SkipInputs`, `Inputs`, `Outputs`).\n- `reusable_workflow.go` — `LocalReusableWorkflowCache` / metadata for local reusable workflows.\n- No separate YAML/JSON data files; data is generated Go source (`scripts/` holds generators).\n\n### 7. Test shapes (read-only observations)\n\n- `config_test.go:12-57` `TestConfigParseSelfHostedRunnerOK` — table of YAML → expected struct field; `config_test.go:59-104` `TestConfigParseError` — table of YAML → substring of error message (e.g. `invalid glob pattern`). **A new config key will likely be tested exactly this way: parse YAML, assert field; and bad input, assert error substring.**\n- `config_test.go:106-151` `TestConfigPathConfigIgnores` — unmarshals `PathConfig` directly and asserts `Ignore.Match`.\n- `config_test.go:153+` `TestConfigIgnoreErrors` — `paths:` glob → ignore behavior.\n- `rule_test.go:10-20` `TestRuleBaseSetGetConfig` — `Config()` nil before `SetConfig`, equal after.\n- `linter_test.go:560-647` — `OnRulesCreated` hook tests that add/remove rules by `r.Name()`; `linter_test.go:649+` default-config-exists test.\n- Rule tests call `rule.VisitJobPre(node)` / `VisitStep(node)` directly with hand-built AST nodes and `rule.SetConfig(&cfg)` (see `rule_runner_label_test.go:322-330`).\n\n### Concrete insertion points for a new config-aware rule\n\n1. **`config.go`** — add a field to `Config` (`config.go:~48-72`), e.g. `ActionPinning struct{...}`; add validation in `ParseConfig` after the `paths` loop (`config.go:97-101`); optionally extend the commented template at `config.go:149-156`.\n2. **New file `rule_<name>.go`** — copy the `rule_permissions.go` skeleton (struct + `NewRuleX()` with `name`/`desc`), add `VisitStep` (for `steps[].uses`) and/or `VisitJobPre` (for `jobs.<id>.uses`), read config through a nil-guarded helper like `rule_runner_label.go:328-333`.\n3. **`linter.go:557-573`** — add `NewRuleX()` to the `rules` literal (config is auto-threaded at `linter.go:608-612`).\n4. **`command.go:~136-150`** + **`linter.go:60-95` / `98-112` / `182-196`** — only if a CLI flag is required.\n5. **`docs/config.md`** and **`docs/checks.md`** — documentation for the new config key / check (docs are not tests; safe to update if the task expects docs).\n\nNo files were modified.' additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 2711, 'prompt_tokens': 41873, 'total_tokens': 44584, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 41728}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 41728, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 145}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-flash', 'system_fingerprint': 'bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6', 'id': '36ee8cf6-fef0-4e4c-8cce-bef5eea76d01', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None} id='lc_run--01a2131f-0ecd-7e50-bcb8-d12ab8ee043a-0' tool_calls=[] invalid_tool_calls=[] usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 41873, 'output_tokens': 2711, 'total_tokens': 44584, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 41728}, 'output_token_details': {}}
