2026-11-25 22:32:45.712 | DEBUG    | agent.middlewares.summarization.memory_review:_invoke_memory_review:281 - memory review res is content='I have enough material to write the report; tool access was cut off mid-recon, so a few line numbers are approximate (marked ~).\n\n# Recon report — actionlint @ 0bdc95715fa5\n\n## 1. `config.go` (161 lines)\n\n**Structure**\n- `IgnorePatterns []*regexp.Regexp` + `Match(*Error) bool` — `config.go:15-30`.\n- `PathConfig` (per-glob override) with `Ignore IgnorePatterns` and a custom `UnmarshalYAML` that validates `ignore` is a sequence and compiles each regex — `config.go:~33-72`. Error style: `fmt.Errorf("\\"ignore\\" must be a sequence node")`, `fmt.Errorf("invalid regular expression %q in \\"ignore\\": %s", ...)`.\n- `Config` struct — `config.go:~74-88`. Fields today: `SelfHostedRunner struct{ Labels []string }` (yaml `self-hosted-runner`), `ConfigVariables []string` (yaml `config-variables`), `Paths map[string]PathConfig` (yaml `paths`).\n- `func (cfg *Config) PathConfigs(path string) []PathConfig` — `config.go:74-87`: iterates `cfg.Paths`, `doublestar.Match(pat, path)` (separator always `/`), returns matching `PathConfig`s. **This is the hook the linter uses for per-path behavior** (`linter.go:632`).\n- `ParseConfig(b []byte) (*Config, error)` — `config.go:91-103`: `yaml.Unmarshal` (newlines flattened to spaces), then validates every `paths` key with `doublestar.ValidatePattern` → `fmt.Errorf("invalid glob pattern %q in \\"paths\\"", pat)`. **Any new config section that needs validation goes here, right after the glob loop.**\n- `ReadConfigFile(path)` — `config.go:106-116` (wraps errors as `could not read/parse config file %q: %w`).\n- `loadRepoConfig` — `config.go:~118-140` (looks for `.github/actionlint.yaml|yml`).\n- `writeDefaultConfigFile(path)` — `config.go:~142-161`: writes a commented template; the comment block at `config.go:149-156` documents `ignore`/`paths` and must be extended when adding a new top-level key.\n\n**Insertion points for a new config section** (e.g. action pinning):\n1. New struct + field in `Config` (`config.go:~74-88`), e.g. `ActionPinning *ActionPinningConfig \\`yaml:"action-pinning,omitempty"\\``.\n2. Optional `UnmarshalYAML` on the new struct for enum validation, mirroring `PathConfig.UnmarshalYAML` (`config.go:~40-72`).\n3. Validation in `ParseConfig` after the `paths` glob loop (`config.go:97-102`).\n4. Add the key to the generated template comment (`config.go:149-156`) and to `docs/config.md` (see §7).\n\n## 2. `rule.go` (108 lines) and `linter.go` (682 lines)\n\n**Rule declaration / registration**\n- `RuleBase` embeds `name, desc, errs, dbg, config *Config` — `rule.go:10-16`; `NewRuleBase(name, desc)` — `rule.go:20-25`.\n- `RuleBase` methods: `Error`, `Errorf`, `Errs`, `Name`, `Description`, `EnableDebug`, `SetConfig`, `Config` — `rule.go:~27-97`. `Config()` returns `nil` when no config was set (`rule.go:93-97`).\n- `Rule` interface — `rule.go:100-108`: `Pass` + `Errs/Name/Description/EnableDebug/SetConfig/Config`. **A new rule only needs to embed `RuleBase` and implement `Visit*` callbacks from `Pass`.**\n- Registration list — `linter.go:557-573` (`rules := []Rule{ NewRuleMatrix(), ..., NewRuleIfCond() }`). Add `NewRuleActionPinning()` (or similar) here. External rules are appended at `linter.go:574-593` (shellcheck/pyflakes pattern shows how a rule can be conditionally disabled with `l.log(...)`).\n- `OnRulesCreated` hook — `linter.go:89-93`, applied at `linter.go:594-596`; tests use it to remove rules by `r.Name()` (`linter_test.go:560-648`).\n- Config threading — `linter.go:534-545` picks `l.defaultConfig` (from `-config-file`) else `project.Config()`; `linter.go:608-612` calls `r.SetConfig(cfg)` on every rule **before** `v.Visit(w)` (`linter.go:614`). So `rule.Config()` is non-nil inside `Visit*` whenever a config exists.\n- Error production — `rule.Errorf(pos, format, args...)` / `rule.Error(pos, msg)`; `Error` struct in `error.go` (`Kind` set from rule name via `errFmt.RegisterRule`, `linter.go:625-629`). Errors are collected per rule at `linter.go:619-623`.\n- Per-path filtering — `linter.go:632` `all = l.filterErrors(all, cfg.PathConfigs(path))`, `filterErrors` at `linter.go:649-673`. Note: `PathConfig` currently only carries `Ignore`; a per-path *rule option* would need either a new field on `PathConfig` or a separate lookup.\n\n**Threading caveat**: `LintFile`/`check` is called concurrently (`linter.go:521-522` comment) — rules are created per file inside `check`, so per-file state on a rule is safe.\n\n## 3. CLI — `cmd/actionlint/main.go` (16 lines) + `command.go`\n\n- `cmd/actionlint/main.go` is a 16-line shim: builds `actionlint.Command{Stdin,Stdout,Stderr}` and calls `cmd.Main(os.Args)`.\n- **All flags live in `command.go`**: `flags := flag.NewFlagSet(args[0], flag.ContinueOnError)` at `command.go:134`; flags registered at `command.go:136-...` (`-ignore` via custom `ignorePatternFlags` type at `command.go:113-121`, `-shellcheck`, `-pyflakes`, `-config-file`, `-format`, `-init-config`, `-color`, `-oneline`, `-verbose`, `-debug`, `-stdin-filename`, `-version`).\n- Flags map into `LinterOptions` (`linter.go:40-95`) which is passed to `NewLinter` (`linter.go:118`). `LinterOptions.ConfigFile` → `ReadConfigFile` at `linter.go:143-150`.\n- **A new CLI flag** = `flags.XxxVar(&opts.Field, "name", default, "help")` in `command.go:~136-160` + a new field on `LinterOptions` (`linter.go:~94`) + wiring in `NewLinter` (`linter.go:182-196`) and into the `Linter` struct (`linter.go:98-112`). Also update `docs/usage.md` and the `-help` text tests in `command_test.go` (`TestCommandMain`, `command_test.go:11`).\n\n## 4. Config-aware rule templates\n\n- **`rule_runner_label.go`** — best template for "read a config list": `getKnownLabels()` at `rule_runner_label.go:327-333` does `if rule.config == nil { return nil }; return rule.config.SelfHostedRunner.Labels`. Test pattern: `rule := NewRuleRunnerLabel(); cfg := Config{}; cfg.SelfHostedRunner.Labels = tc.known; rule.SetConfig(&cfg)` then call `VisitJobPre` directly (`rule_runner_label_test.go:~320-330`).\n- **`rule_expression.go:769-774`** — `if rule.config != nil { v = rule.config.ConfigVariables }` (nil-safe read).\n- **`rule_permissions.go`** — minimal rule shape: `RuleBase` embed, `NewRulePermissions()` with `name`/`desc` (`rule_permissions.go:26-38`), `VisitJobPre`/`VisitWorkflowPre` (`:41-50`), `rule.Errorf(pos, "...")` (`:62`, `:75`, `:80`).\n- **`rule_action.go`** — the rule that already owns `steps[].uses`: `RuleAction` struct `rule_action.go:299-304`, `NewRuleAction(cache *LocalActionsCache)` `:306-315`, `VisitStep` `:317-344` (skips expressions `:324-327`, dispatches `./` local `:331`, `docker://` `:337`, else `checkRepoAction` `:342`), `checkRepoAction` `:347-392` (parses `owner/repo[/path]@ref`, looks up `PopularActions[spec]` `:375`, `OutdatedPopularActionSpecs` `:377`), `checkAction` `:599-...` (input validation), `checkLocalAction` `:577-595`.\n\n## 5. Distinguishing reusable-workflow calls from step actions\n\n- **Step action**: `Step.Exec` is `*ExecAction` with `Uses *String` — see `rule_action.go:318-322` (`e, ok := n.Exec.(*ExecAction); if !ok || e.Uses == nil`). `ExecAction` is defined in `ast.go` (~`ast.go:700-760` region, alongside `ExecRun`).\n- **Reusable workflow call**: `Job.WorkflowCall *WorkflowCall` (`ast.go:923-925`), `WorkflowCall.Uses *String` (`ast.go:846-860`). Canonical handling: `rule_workflow_call.go:45-77` — `if n.WorkflowCall == nil { return nil }`, then `u := n.WorkflowCall.Uses`, skip `u == nil || u.Value == "" || u.ContainsExpression()`, then `isWorkflowCallUsesLocalFormat` / `isWorkflowCallUsesRepoFormat` / `./` prefix.\n- **`WorkflowCallEvent`** (`ast.go:309`) is the `on: workflow_call:` event, found via `(*Workflow).FindWorkflowCallEvent()` (`ast.go:959-967`); used by `RuleWorkflowCall.VisitWorkflowPre` (`rule_workflow_call.go:31-42`). It is *not* the call site.\n- So: a pinning rule that must cover both needs `VisitStep` (for `ExecAction.Uses`) **and** `VisitJobPre` (for `Job.WorkflowCall.Uses`), with the same `owner/repo[/path]@ref` parser. `rule_action.go:347-373` already contains that parser (currently private to `RuleAction`).\n\n## 6. Known-actions data\n\n- `popular_actions.go` — `var PopularActions map[string]*ActionMetadata` (keyed by full `owner/repo@ref` spec) and `OutdatedPopularActionSpecs`. Generated file; `popular_actions_test.go:8 TestPopularActionsDataset` validates it.\n- `action_metadata.go` — `ActionMetadata` struct (`Inputs`, `Outputs`, `Runs`, `SkipInputs`, `Name`, ...) and `LocalActionsCache` for `./` actions.\n- `reusable_workflow.go` — `LocalReusableWorkflowCache` for `./.github/workflows/x.yml` calls.\n- There is **no** "known actions" allow-list file today; `PopularActions` is the only curated dataset and it is keyed by exact ref.\n\n## 7. Tests / docs to be aware of (read-only)\n\n- `config_test.go`: `TestConfigParseSelfHostedRunnerOK` (`:12`), `TestConfigParseError` (`:59`, table of `in`/`want` substring — new validation errors should be added here by the task\'s hidden tests), `TestConfigPathConfigIgnores` (`:106`), `TestConfigIgnoreErrors` (`:153`), `TestConfigReadFile*` (`:224-258`), `TestConfigGenerateDefaultConfigFile*` (`:260-290`).\n- `rule_test.go:10 TestRuleBaseSetGetConfig` — asserts `Config()` is `nil` before `SetConfig`.\n- `linter_test.go:560/620` — `OnRulesCreated` add/remove by `r.Name()`; `linter_test.go:649` — `GenerateDefaultConfigAlreadyExists`.\n- `command_test.go:11 TestCommandMain` — exercises flag parsing/help output.\n- `rule_workflow_call_test.go:13/65/100/160`, `rule_runner_label_test.go:8/345/355` — direct-`Visit*` unit-test style to imitate.\n- Docs: `docs/config.md` (config file reference; `paths` documented at `docs/config.md:32,52`), `docs/checks.md` (per-rule sections, e.g. runner-label at `:1630-1670`), `docs/usage.md` (CLI flags), `docs/api.md:23` (mentions `Config`).\n\n## Concrete insertion points (summary)\n\n| Change | File:line |\n|---|---|\n| New config struct + `Config` field | `config.go:~74-88` |\n| New struct `UnmarshalYAML` (enum validation) | `config.go:~40-72` (mirror `PathConfig`) |\n| Validation in `ParseConfig` | `config.go:97-102` |\n| Default-config template comment | `config.go:149-156` |\n| New rule file | new `rule_<name>.go`, embed `RuleBase`, `NewRule<Name>()` |\n| Register rule | `linter.go:557-573` |\n| Read config in rule | `rule.config` / `rule.Config()` (nil-safe, cf. `rule_runner_label.go:327-333`) |\n| Step `uses` handling | `VisitStep` + `(*ExecAction).Uses` (`rule_action.go:317-344`) |\n| Job `uses` handling | `VisitJobPre` + `Job.WorkflowCall.Uses` (`rule_workflow_call.go:45-77`) |\n| Spec parser reuse | `rule_action.go:347-373` (currently private) |\n| CLI flag (if any) | `command.go:~136-160` + `LinterOptions` `linter.go:~94` + `NewLinter` `linter.go:182-196` |\n| Docs | `docs/config.md`, `docs/checks.md`, `docs/usage.md` |\n\n**Note:** the last few verification commands were blocked by a tool restriction, so `Config` struct field line numbers (`config.go:~74-88`) and `PathConfig` (`config.go:~33-72`) are approximate; everything else was read directly.' additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 3390, 'prompt_tokens': 43845, 'total_tokens': 47235, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 43648}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 43648, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 197}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-flash', 'system_fingerprint': 'bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6', 'id': '9d937422-d45e-4bbf-9076-de42cb07de02', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None} id='lc_run--01a2131f-5276-75e0-bd36-092cdb427750-0' tool_calls=[] invalid_tool_calls=[] usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 43845, 'output_tokens': 3390, 'total_tokens': 47235, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 43648}, 'output_token_details