TestRuleRunnerLabelCheckLabels` — **canonical config-aware rule test**: table `{labels []string; expected []string}`; per case `cfg := Config{}; cfg.SelfHostedRunner.Labels = tc.known; rule.SetConfig(&cfg)`, then `rule.VisitJobPre(node)` and compare `rule.Errs()` messages (assertion block ~lines 320–340).\n- `rule_workflow_call_test.go:13` `TestRuleWorkflowCallCheckWorkflowCallUsesFormat` — builds `&Job{WorkflowCall: &WorkflowCall{Uses: &String{Value: tc.uses, Pos: &Pos{}}}}`, calls `r.VisitJobPre(j)`, compares `r.Errs()`.\n- `rule_workflow_call_test.go:65` `TestRuleWorkflowCallNestedWorkflowCalls`; `:100` `TestRuleWorkflowCallWriteEventNodeToMetadataCache`; `:160` `TestRuleWorkflowCallCheckReusableWorkflowCall` (uses `LocalReusableWorkflowCache` + temp dirs).\n- `rule_env_var_test.go:21/39/55`; `rule_id_test.go:8/72`; `rule_glob_test.go`, `rule_if_cond_test.go`, `rule_deprecated_commands_test.go` — all follow the same `VisitXxx` + `Errs()` shape.\n- **No dedicated test file for `RuleAction` or `RulePermissions`** — they are covered indirectly via `linter_test.go` (`TestLinterLintOK:28`, `TestLinterLintError:155`, `AllErrorWorkflowsAtOnce:218`, `TestLinterLintProject:313`) and `testdata/err/`, `testdata/ok/`.\n\n### Linter / CLI tests\n- `linter_test.go:560` `TestLinterAddCustomRuleOnRulesCreatedHook` (sets `l.defaultConfig = &Config{}`), `:620` `TestLinterRemoveRuleOnRulesCreatedHook`, `:649` `GenerateDefaultConfigAlreadyExists`.\n- `command_test.go:11` `TestCommandMain` — CLI flag behavior.\n- `popular_actions_test.go:8` `TestPopularActionsDataset`; `action_metadata_test.go:83+` local-action cache tests.\n- Fixtures: `testdata/config/{ok.yml,broken.yml,projects/}`, `testdata/err/`, `testdata/ok/`, `testdata/examples/`, `testdata/reusable_workflow_metadata/`.\n\n## 2. `insertion_points` (concrete, with anchors)\n\n### A. New config key\n1. **`config.go:48-52`** — `type PathConfig struct { Ignore IgnorePatterns \\`yaml:"ignore"\\` }`. Add per-path fields here (e.g. `ActionPinning` / allow-list) with a `yaml:"..."` tag.\n2. **`config.go:56-70`** — `type Config struct`: `SelfHostedRunner` (58-61), `ConfigVariables` (66), `Paths map[string]PathConfig` (69). Add a **global** field here if the option is not per-path (mirror `ConfigVariables []string`).\n3. **`config.go:17-44`** — `IgnorePatterns` + its `UnmarshalYAML` is the template for a custom-validating config type. Error style: `fmt.Errorf("yaml: \\"ignore\\" must be a sequence node at line:%d,col:%d", ...)` and `fmt.Errorf("invalid regular expression %q in \\"ignore\\" at line%d,col:%d: %w", ...)`.\n4. **`config.go:91-103`** `ParseConfig` — after `yaml.Unmarshal`, the validation loop at **97-101** currently only checks `paths` globs (`fmt.Errorf("invalid glob pattern %q in \\"paths\\"", pat)`). Extend it to validate new values in the same style.\n5. **`config.go:136-161`** `writeDefaultConfigFile` — the raw template string emitted by `-init-config`; add the new key here (asserted verbatim by `config_test.go:260`).\n6. **`config.go:74-87`** `PathConfigs(path)` — nil-safe, `filepath.ToSlash` + `doublestar.MatchUnvalidated`; returns `[]PathConfig` for a file path. This is the accessor a per-path rule should use.\n\n### B. New config-aware rule\n7. **New file `rule_<name>.go`** — skeleton modeled on `rule_runner_label.go` / `rule_permissions.go`:\n   ```go\n   type RuleActionPinning struct { RuleBase }\n   func NewRuleActionPinning() *RuleActionPinning {\n       return &RuleActionPinning{RuleBase: NewRuleBase("action-pinning", "....")}\n   }\n   // steps[].uses  — mirror rule_action.go:318-344\n   func (rule *RuleActionPinning) VisitStep(n *Step) error {\n       e, ok := n.Exec.(*ExecAction)\n       if !ok || e.Uses == nil || e.Uses.ContainsExpression() { return nil }\n       ...\n       rule.Errorf(e.Uses.Pos, ".... %q ....", e.Uses.Value)   // rule.go:44-54\n       return nil\n   }\n   // jobs.<id>.uses — mirror rule_workflow_call.go:45-77\n   func (rule *RuleActionPinning) VisitJobPre(n *Job) error {\n       if n.WorkflowCall == nil { return nil }\n       u := n.WorkflowCall.Uses\n       if u == nil || u.Value == "" || u.ContainsExpression() { return nil }\n       ...\n   }\n   ```\n   `SetConfig`/`Config` come free from `RuleBase` (`rule.go:89-97`); **always nil-check `rule.config`** (see `rule_runner_label.go:328-333`, `rule_expression.go:770-773`) because `linter.go:608-612` only calls `SetConfig` when a config file exists.\n8. **`linter.go:557-573`** — append `NewRuleActionPinning()` to the `rules := []Rule{...}` literal (or pass `path` / `cfg.PathConfigs(path)` like `NewRuleWorkflowCall(path, localReusableWorkflows)` at 569).\n9. **`linter.go:608-612`** — config threading: `if cfg != nil { for _, r := range rules { r.SetConfig(cfg) } }`. No change needed; note the **nil-config caveat**.\n10. **`linter.go:632`** + **`linter.go:649-673`** `filterErrors` — per-path consumption path: `all = l.filterErrors(all, cfg.PathConfigs(path))`; `filterErrors` applies CLI `-ignore` first, then each `PathConfig.Ignore.Match(err)`. Extend here if the new option is a suppression rather than a diagnostic.\n11. **`command.go:134-148`** — CLI flags (`flag.NewFlagSet`, `flags.StringVar(&opts.ConfigFile, "config-file", ...)` at 141); map any new flag into `LinterOptions` (`linter.go:53-95`), the `Linter` struct (`linter.go:98-112`) and `NewLinter` (`linter.go:118-200`). `cmd/actionlint/main.go` is a 16-line shim — no changes needed there.\n12. **Docs**: `docs/config.md` (paths section), `docs/checks.md` (new rule section), `CHANGELOG.md`.\n\n### C. AST anchors for the two `uses` sites\n- `Step.Exec Exec` — `ast.go:737`; `*ExecAction.Uses *String` — `ast.go` (`ExecAction` struct).\n- `Job.WorkflowCall *WorkflowCall` — `ast.go:925`; `WorkflowCall.Uses *String` — `ast.go:848-850`.\n- `WorkflowCallEvent` — `ast.go:309`, found via `Workflow.FindWorkflowCallEvent()` (`ast.go:960-967`).\n- Known-actions data: `popular_actions.go:7` `PopularActions map[string]*ActionMetadata`, `:4289` `OutdatedPopularActionSpecs`; `ActionMetadata` at `action_metadata.go:157-179`. No separate allow-list file exists.\n\n## 3. Open questions / ambiguities\n1. **Global vs per-path**: should the new option live in `Config` (global, like `config-variables`) or in `PathConfig` (per-path, like `ignore`)? The `paths:` mechanism only supports `ignore` today, so a per-path option needs both a new `PathConfig` field and a new consumption site (rule constructor arg vs `filterErrors`).\n2. **Diagnostic vs suppression**: does the new behavior emit an `Error` (rule) or filter existing errors (`filterErrors`)? This decides whether it is a `Rule` at all.\n3. **Scope of `uses`**: should reusable-workflow calls (`jobs.<id>.uses`) be checked by the same rule as step actions (`steps[].uses`), or only steps? They are distinct AST nodes, so either is easy — but the rule name/description and docs must state it.\n4. **Local/docker specs**: `./path` and `docker://` are handled separately in `rule_action.go:331-340`; confirm whether they are exempt.\n5. **Default-config output**: adding a key to `writeDefaultConfigFile` changes `-init-config` output, which `config_test.go:260` asserts verbatim — decide whether the key is emitted by default (commented out vs active).\n6. **Nil config**: rules receive `nil` when no config file is present; the default behavior with no config must be defined (no-op vs default policy).' additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 2748, 'prompt_tokens': 31945, 'total_tokens': 34693, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 31744}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 31744, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 201}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-flash', 'system_fingerprint': 'bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6', 'id': '0c3b34b0-05e4-4671-91f5-5be232e65cc5', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None} id='lc_run--01a21320-c60e-7d12-89