ocal, `docker://`, and expression-containing refs.\n   - `rule_workflow_call.go` `isWorkflowCallUsesRepoFormat` gives the reusable-workflow `owner/repo/path@ref` parser.\n   - `error.go`: `Error{Message, Filepath, Line, Column, Kind}` and `RuleBase.Errorf(pos, format, args...)`.\n\n### What remains to be written (ready to apply once writes are permitted)\n\n- **`config.go`**: add `ActionPinningLevel` (+ constants/`IsValid`/`String`), `ActionPinningConfig`, `PathConfig.ActionPinning`, `Config.ActionPinning`, `MergeActionPinningConfigs`, `ActionPinningConfigForPath`, `validateActionPinningConfig`, `validateAllowedDenied`, and wire validation into `ParseConfig`.\n- **`action_pinning_rule.go`**: `RuleActionPinning` with `VisitStep` (step actions) and `VisitJobPre` (reusable workflows), regexes for `vX.Y` / `vX.Y.Z` / 40-hex SHA, allowed/denied owner+action checks, per-path config via `ActionPinningConfigForPath`, and messages that say "step action" vs "reusable workflow" and include the offending ref + expected level.\n- **`rule.go`**: `NewRuleActionPinning()` constructor + name `action-pinning`.\n- **`linter.go`**: append the rule to the default `rules` slice.\n\n**To proceed, please re-run this task with write access enabled** (exit background-review mode). I have the full design ready and can apply it in a handful of edits, then run `go build ./...` and `python -m pytest -q` (or `go test ./...`) once to verify.' additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 851, 'prompt_tokens': 46978, 'total_tokens': 47829, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 46720}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 46720, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 258}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-flash', 'system_fingerprint': 'bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6', 'id': '0deb96f2-02fd-4c99-bffa-91bce4a0ae9b', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None} id='lc_run--01a21325-e5b3-7210-87e4-