ter the `action` entry), and the surrounding `"rules"` array plus any `"index"` references in `results` must stay consistent.\n\n### On the `cmd/actionlint/main.go` question — explicit note\n\n**The flag registration in `command.go` is the correct equivalent of the requested `cmd/actionlint/main.go` change.** In this repository, `cmd/actionlint/main.go` is a thin shim that only calls `actionlint.Command{...}.Main(os.Args)`. All CLI flag parsing — every existing flag (`-config-file`, `-format`, `-ignore`, `-stdin-filename`, `-init-config`, `-color`, …) — lives in `Command.Main` in `command.go`. Adding the flag to `main.go` would be architecturally wrong and would not be reachable by the `Command` API or its tests. So `-action-pinning-level` was registered with `flags.Var(&pinningLevel, "action-pinning-level", ...)` in `command.go`, which is the same place and mechanism as every other flag.\n\n### Verification already completed (prior turns)\n\n- `go build ./...` → **BUILD_OK**\n- `go vet ./...` → **VET_OK**\n- `-action-pinning-level bogus` → exit **2** (`ExitStatusInvalidCommandOption`) with `invalid value "bogus" for -action-pinning-level option: available values are "major-minor", "semver", "commit-sha"` plus usage\n- `major-minor`, `semver`, `commit-sha` → all exit **0**\n- `go test . ./cmd/...` → root package `ok` except the SARIF fixture test\n- `go test ./...` → only the three `scripts/generate-*` packages fail, identically on the pristine tree (no network in sandbox)\n\n### Remaining work\n\n1. Update `testdata/format/test.sarif` with the `action-pinning` rule descriptor.\n2. Re-run `go test -count=1 . ./cmd/...` to confirm green.\n\nI was unable to execute these final two steps because tool execution was blocked in this turn.' additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 913, 'prompt_tokens': 36748, 'total_tokens': 37661, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_t