2026-11-25 22:45:55.237 | DEBUG    | agent.middlewares.summarization.memory_review:_invoke_memory_review:281 - memory review res is content="I'm blocked from further tool use (a background review is in progress), so here is the state and the remaining item.\n\n## What's done\n\n**Flag registration & validation** — `command.go` (correct location; `cmd/actionlint/main.go` has no flag parsing):\n- `-action-pinning-level` registered with values `major-minor`, `semver`, `commit-sha`; invalid values produce a usage error listing the accepted values.\n- Value is stored on `LinterOptions` and threaded into `Linter` (`linter.go`), then applied in `Linter.check` after rule creation: for every `*RuleActionPinning`, `SetActionPinningLevelOverride(level)` is called, which overrides both the config-file level and per-path overrides (and enables the rule even if config disabled it).\n\n**Precedence wiring** — `action_pinning_rule.go`: `levelOverride` is consulted first in `configuredLevel()`/`actionPinningConfig()`, ahead of path-specific and global config.\n\n**Test suite** — `go build ./...` and `go vet ./...` clean; `go test .` passes except `TestLinterFormatErrorMessageInSARIF`. The only remaining failures elsewhere are the pre-existing network-dependent `scripts/generate-*` tests (`dial tcp ... network is unreachable`), unrelated to this change.\n\n## The SARIF fixture issue (feedback item 2)\n\nThe mismatch is **not** from a stale fixture edit — `testdata/format/test.sarif` was unmodified in the working tree. It fails because step-2's new rule is registered in the linter, so the SARIF output now contains an extra `action-pinning` rule descriptor that the golden fixture lacks. I added that descriptor to the fixture (matching the rule's `name`/`desc`/`helpUri`), but the test still reports the entry as missing from `have`, which suggests the SARIF rule list is emitted in a different order or filtered by something I couldn't inspect before tool access was cut off. Two options for whoever picks this up:\n\n1. **Preferred per the step's instruction**: revert my `testdata/format/test.sarif` edit (`git checkout -- testdata/format/test.sarif`) and treat the SARIF golden mismatch as fallout of step-2's rule registration, to be fixed in that step (regenerate the fixture there).\n2. If it must be fixed here: inspect `Linter.generateSARIF` to see how the rule list is built/ordered and place the `action-pinning` descriptor accordingly.\n\n## Still to do (feedback item 1)\n\nThe end-to-end precedence proof was not run. Suggested commands:\n\n```bash\ngo build -o /tmp/actionlint ./cmd/actionlint\nmkdir -p /tmp/e2e && cd /tmp/e2e\ncat > .github/actionlint.yaml <<'EOF'\naction-pinning:\n  level: semver\nEOF\ncat > wf.yaml <<'EOF'\non: push\njobs:\n  test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@8e5e7e5e4c1b2b3c4d5e6f708192a3b4c5d6e7f8  # SHA only\nEOF\n/tmp/actionlint -action-pinning-level commit-sha wf.yaml   # expect: no error (flag wins over semver)\n/tmp/actionlint wf.yaml                                    # expect: error (config semver rejects SHA)\n```\n\nRepeat with a `paths:`-scoped `action-pinning` block to show per-path config is also overridden." additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 789, 'prompt_tokens': 25406, 'total_tokens': 26195, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 25216}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 25216, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 190}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-flash', 'system_fingerprint': 'bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6', 'id': '2531911c-f39f-4953-849e-2bf1cf4a861f', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None} id='lc_run--01a2132b-8aed-79c3-84d1-3f8829de36ed-0' tool_calls=[] invalid_tool_calls=[] usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 25406, 'output_tokens': 789, 'total_tokens': 26195, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 25216}, 'output_token_details': {}}
