2026-11-25 22:52:44.837 | DEBUG    | agent.middlewares.summarization.memory_review:_invoke_memory_review:281 - memory review res is content='All tools are now blocked (background review mode), so I\'ll report with the evidence already gathered.\n\n# Review Report — `action-pinning` rule (commit 1945d8d, branch `feature/action-pinning-rule`)\n\n## Build / test results\n| Command | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `gofmt -l .` | **PASS** — no output (clean) |\n| `go vet ./...` | **PASS** — no output |\n| `go build ./...` | **PASS** — no output |\n| `go test -count=1 . ./cmd/... ./scripts/check-checks` | **PASS** — `ok github.com/rhysd/actionlint 0.162s`, `ok .../scripts/check-checks 0.019s`, `cmd/actionlint [no test files]` |\n| `git show --stat HEAD` | **PASS** — 7 files, all non-test: `action_pinning_rule.go`, `command.go`, `config.go`, `docs/checks.md`, `docs/config.md`, `linter.go`, `testdata/format/test.sarif`. **No `*_test.go` modified.** |\n\n## Acceptance checklist\n\n**1. Config section + `level` values — PASS**\n`config.go` adds `ActionPinningLevel` with `major-minor`/`semver`/`commit-sha`; patterns at `action_pinning_rule.go:48-52`: `^v\\d+\\.\\d+$`, `^v\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+(-[0-9A-Za-z.-]+)?(\\+[0-9A-Za-z.-]+)?$` (prerelease+build), `^[0-9a-f]{40}$` (lowercase only). Empirically: `v4` fails at `major-minor`; `v4.1.7` and `v4.1.7-rc.1` pass at `semver`; uppercase 40-hex SHA fails at `commit-sha`; lowercase 40-hex passes. Default `semver` confirmed (`action-pinning: {}` → 4 errors, same as explicit `semver`).\n\n**2. Increasing strictness ordering — PASS**\n`isPinned` (`action_pinning_rule.go:255-275`) is cumulative: `major-minor` accepts major-minor ∨ semver ∨ SHA; `semver` accepts semver ∨ SHA; `commit-sha` accepts SHA only. Verified: SHA ref passes at `major-minor` and `semver`, fails at `commit-sha`; `v4.1.7` passes at `major-minor`, fails at `commit-sha`.\n\n**3. Dynamic version ref → error; dynamic action name → skip — PASS**\n`action_pinning_rule.go:107` skips when the action name contains an expression; `:200-206` emits `"... is not pinned because its version reference is a dynamic expression which cannot be verified for pinning"`. Verified: `actions/checkout@${{ matrix.ref }}` errors; `${{ matrix.action }}@v1` produces no error.\n\n**4. `allowed-owners` (case-insensitive), `allowed-actions`, `denied-owners`, `denied-actions` — PASS**\n`isExempted` (`action_pinning_rule.go:227-236`) uses `containsFold` (`:278-285`, `strings.EqualFold`) for all four lists. Verified: `allowed-owners: [ACTIONS]` exempts `actions/checkout`; `allowed-actions: [actions/checkout]` exempts it.\n\n**5. Union merge of global + per-path lists — PASS**\nVerified: global `allowed-owners: [actions]` + path `allowed-owners: [octo]` → 0 errors (both exempted). Global `denied-owners: [actions]` + path `allowed-owners: [actions]` → 6 errors (deny from global still applies). Path `level` overrides global level (6 errors vs 4).\n\n**6. Denials take precedence; denied entries still checked — PASS**\n`isExempted` returns `false` immediately on deny match before consulting allow lists (`action_pinning_rule.go:230-233`). Verified: `allowed-owners: [actions]` + `denied-owners: [Actions]` → 6 errors (not exempted, still pinning-checked); same for `allowed-actions`/`denied-actions`.\n\n**7. `-action-pinning-level` flag — PASS**\n`command.go` adds the flag with validation (`invalid value "bogus" ... available values are "major-minor", "semver", "commit-sha"`); `linter.go:606-614` applies `SetActionPinningLevelOverride` to every `RuleActionPinning` after rule creation. `configuredLevel()` (`action_pinning_rule.go:70-79`) returns the override first, so it enables the rule even when config is `null`. Verified: `action-pinning: null` + flag → 4 errors; config `level: major-minor` + `allowed-owners: [Actions]` + flag `commit-sha` → only the non-exempt reusable workflow errors (allow list preserved, level overridden).\n\n**8. Config validation — PASS**\nAll rejected with clear messages: invalid `level` (global and per-path), `allowed-owners: ["a/b"]`, `denied-owners: ["a/b"]` ("owner name must not be empty and must not contain \'/\'"), `allowed-actions: ["norepo"]`, `denied-actions: ["a/b/c"]` ("action must be in \\"{owner}/{repo}\\" format"), and per-path variants.\n\n**9. `null` disabled / `{}` enabled / per-path enables — PASS**\n`action-pinning: null` → 0 errors; `action-pinning: {}` → 4 errors (default semver); no section → 0 errors; per-path-only `action-pinning` (no global) → 6 errors (rule enabled).\n\n**10. Skip local/Docker; message distinguishes workflows; known-actions suggestions — PASS (with one caveat)**\n`action_pinning_rule.go:95-98` skips `./` and `docker://`. Messages use `kind` = `step action` vs `reusable workflow` (verified both in output). `knownVersionSuggestion` (`:238-256`) scans `PopularActions` for a ref satisfying the level. **Caveat:** in my test the suggestion suffix did not appear for `actions/checkout@v4` at `semver` even though `actions/checkout@v4` exists in `popular_actions.go:540` — the suggestion is only appended when a *known* ref satisfies the level, and `v4` itself does not satisfy `semver`, so no suggestion is emitted. This is consistent with the code\'s intent (suggest a known ref that *does* satisfy the level), but it means the "known-actions data is used for version suggestions" behavior is only observable when a satisfying known ref exists (e.g. `v4.1.7`-style entries). Not a contract violation, but worth noting as a weak spot in the suggestion coverage.\n\n## intent_match: **yes**\n\n## intent_deviations\n- **Minor:** Known-version suggestion is silent for common major-only refs (`@v4`) at `semver`/`commit-sha` levels because no known ref in `PopularActions` satisfies those levels for that action. The contract says "Known-actions data is used for version suggestions" — the mechanism exists and is wired, but its practical coverage is limited. No functional bug.\n- **Minor:** `testdata/format/test.sarif` was modified by the commit (adds the `action-pinning` rule descriptor). This is a generated fixture, not a test file, and is required for the SARIF format test to pass — acceptable, but it is fixture churn that reviewers should be aware of.\n- No `*_test.go` files were added or modified, so the new rule has **no dedicated unit tests** in this commit. The contract did not require tests, but coverage is via existing integration/format tests only.\n\n## Verdict\nAll 8 acceptance-checklist items **PASS**, all 10 contract items **PASS** (item 10 with the noted suggestion-coverage caveat). Build, vet, gofmt, and the specified test suites are green, and no test files were touched.' additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 1870, 'prompt_tokens': 30457, 'total_tokens': 32327, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 30208}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 30208, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 249}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-flash', 'system_fingerprint': 'bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6', 'id': '3b94f1ac-5aea-4013-9961-4a194cf06cff', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None} id='lc_run--01a21331-b9e9-73b0-a1e9-1c0f43bb4ea2-0' tool_calls=[] invalid_tool_calls=[] usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 30457, 'output_tokens': 1870, 'total_tokens': 32327, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 30208}, 'output_token_details': {}}
