2026-11-26 01:42:38.872 | DEBUG    | agent.middlewares.summarization.memory_review:_invoke_memory_review:281 - memory review res is content='I\'m currently in a restricted review context where file and terminal tools are blocked, so I can\'t inspect or edit further right now. Here\'s the accurate state and the one remaining fix.\n\n## Repo state (verified before tools were restricted)\n\n`git status` showed all five targets modified, and `python -m pytest -q` passed (8 passed).\n\n| File | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `aiomonitor/types.py` | ✅ `Snapshot`, `SnapshotSummary`, `SnapshotDiff` dataclasses added |\n| `aiomonitor/monitor.py` | ✅ `max_snapshots` on `__init__`/`start_monitor`, `capture_snapshot`, `list_snapshots`, `get_snapshot`, `delete_snapshot`, `format_snapshot_task_list`, `format_snapshot_terminated_task_list`, `format_snapshot_task_stack`, `format_snapshot_diff` |\n| `aiomonitor/termui/commands.py` | ⚠️ `snapshot` group + `save/list(ls)/show/where/diff/delete` present, but **group callback is broken** |\n| `aiomonitor/webui/app.py` | ✅ 6 routes + `/snapshots` nav item + page handler |\n| `aiomonitor/webui/templates/snapshots.html` | ✅ created |\n\n## The one remaining bug\n\nMy end-to-end verification confirmed the **entire core contract passes** (ids, eviction order, `KeyError`s, `\'-\'` preservation, header items, diff by `int(task_id)`, `start_monitor(max_snapshots=5)`), and every CLI subcommand works. The single failure is invoking the bare `snapshot` group:\n\n```\nTypeError: snapshot_group() missing 1 required positional argument: \'ctx\'\n```\n\nDiagnosis: the decorator stack is\n\n```python\n@monitor_cli.group(name="snapshot", cls=AliasGroupMixin, add_help_option=False)\n@custom_help_option\n@auto_command_done\n@click.pass_context\ndef snapshot_group(ctx): ...\n```\n\n`auto_command_done` wraps the callback in a zero-arg `wrapper()` that calls the inner function with no arguments, so `click.pass_context`\'s `ctx` never gets injected. The innermost function does have `ctx`; the middle wrapper drops it.\n\n**Fix:** drop `@click.pass_context` and take no `ctx` parameter, matching how other groups in this file are written:\n\n```python\n@monitor_cli.group(name="snapshot", cls=AliasGroupMixin, add_help_option=False)\n@custom_help_option\n@auto_command_done\ndef snapshot_group() -> None:\n    """Manage task snapshots"""\n    click.echo(snapshot_group.get_help(click.get_current_context()))\n```\n\n(If `get_help` needs the context, `click.get_current_context()` retrieves it without a parameter.)\n\n## What I could not finish\n\nI could not apply that edit or re-run `python -m pytest -q` because `read_file`, `search_files`, and `terminal` are all blocked in this review context. The existing suite passed before this point and this change only touches the group callback signature, so it should not affect the 8 passing tests — but **the fix is unapplied and unverified**. Please re-run me in a normal context (or apply the snippet above) to close it out.' additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 737, 'prompt_tokens': 44018, 'total_tokens': 44755, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 43776}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 43776, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 242}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-flash', 'system_fingerprint': 'bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6', 'id': '91e8619c-bee7-470b-b92a-0fb4205c60fc', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None} id='lc_run--01a213cd-4fbf-7d42-bf76-12edeeb72548-0' tool_calls=[] invalid_tool_calls=[] usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 44018, 'output_tokens': 737, 'total_tokens': 44755, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 43776}, 'output_token_details': {}}
