2026-11-26 01:47:36.286 | DEBUG    | agent.middlewares.summarization.memory_review:_invoke_memory_review:281 - memory review res is content="I'm now in a background review context where tools are restricted. Let me report the state based on what I've verified.\n\n## Summary of work completed\n\n**Files changed (all 5 required):**\n\n1. **`aiomonitor/types.py`** — Added `Snapshot` (id, name, created_at, running_tasks, terminated_tasks, running_stacks, terminated_stacks, running_task_ids), `SnapshotSummary` (id, name, created_at, running_count, terminated_count), and `SnapshotDiff` (added, removed, common) dataclasses; imported `Dict`/`field`.\n\n2. **`aiomonitor/monitor.py`** — Added `max_snapshots: int = 10` to `Monitor.__init__` and `start_monitor`; initialized `_snapshots`, `_max_snapshots`, `_next_snapshot_id`; added `max_snapshots` property, `_normalize_snapshot_id`, `capture_snapshot` (freezes running/terminated lists + per-task stacks with failure guards, unnamed-first eviction), `list_snapshots`, `get_snapshot`, `delete_snapshot`, `format_snapshot_task_list`, `format_snapshot_terminated_task_list`, `format_snapshot_task_stack`, and `format_snapshot_diff` (diff by `int(task_id)`).\n\n3. **`aiomonitor/termui/commands.py`** — Added `snapshot` click group (`AliasGroupMixin`, `custom_help_option`, `auto_command_done`) with `save` (`--name`), `list`/`ls`, `show`, `where`, `diff`, `delete`; `save` uses `asyncio.run_coroutine_threadsafe` + `asyncio.wrap_future` on the monitored loop; invalid IDs caught as `KeyError` → `print_fail`.\n\n4. **`aiomonitor/webui/app.py`** — Added `SnapshotIdParams`/`SnapshotSaveParams`/`SnapshotTaskParams`/`SnapshotDiffParams`, handlers for `POST /api/snapshot/save`, `GET /api/snapshot/list`, `POST /api/snapshot/tasks`, `POST /api/snapshot/trace`, `POST /api/snapshot/diff`, `DELETE /api/snapshot` (404 missing / 400 invalid), `/snapshots` page route, and the `/snapshots` nav item.\n\n5. **`aiomonitor/webui/templates/snapshots.html`** — New page with save form, snapshot list, and delete actions.\n\n**Verification status:**\n- `python -m pytest -q` → **8 passed** (existing suite green).\n- Core contract smoke test passed: id auto-increment from 1, unnamed-first eviction, `list_snapshots` summaries, `get_snapshot`/`delete_snapshot` `KeyError`, `format_snapshot_task_stack` `KeyError` on missing task, `format_snapshot_diff` by task id, `start_monitor(max_snapshots=5)`.\n- CLI group registers all 6 subcommands correctly (`save`, `list`, `show`, `where`, `diff`, `delete`).\n\n**Remaining issue (unresolved):** The `snapshot` group's own callback (bare `snapshot` / `snapshot --help`) raised `snapshot_group() missing 1 required positional argument: 'ctx'` in my earlier smoke test. The subcommands themselves work. The likely fix is that `AliasGroupMixin.group()` does not inject `click.pass_context`, so the group callback needs `@click.pass_context` applied *innermost* (closest to the function) — i.e. the decorator order must be `@monitor_cli.group(...)` / `@custom_help_option` / `@auto_command_done` / `@click.pass_context` with `pass_context` directly above `def`. I was unable to re-verify this fix because tool execution became restricted mid-review.\n\n**Recommended next step:** Confirm the decorator order on `snapshot_group` in `commands.py` (pass_context innermost), then re-run the CLI smoke test for `snapshot` with no subcommand and `snapshot --help`, followed by `python -m pytest -q`." additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 942, 'prompt_tokens': 69291, 'total_tokens': 70233, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 69120}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 69120, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 171}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-flash', 'system_fingerprint': 'bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6', 'id': 'ecd6f800-7450-44bf-9631-016d2b565922', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None} i