rrently the **outermost** decorator, but it must be **innermost** (directly above `def snapshot_group`) so the `Context` is injected before `@auto_command_done`\'s wrapper runs. The fix is to reorder to:\n\n```python\n@monitor_cli.group(name="snapshot", cls=AliasGroupMixin, add_help_option=False)\n@custom_help_option\n@auto_command_done\n@click.pass_context\ndef snapshot_group(ctx: click.Context) -> None:\n    """Manage task snapshots"""\n    click.echo(snapshot_group.get_help(ctx))\n```\n\ni.e. move `@click.pass_context` to the line immediately above `def`, below `@auto_command_done`. (The subcommands themselves are unaffected — they already use the correct order and their `save`/`list`/`show`/`where`/`diff`/`delete` paths were exercised successfully.)\n\n**Note:** the existing test suite passes (8/8) because it does not exercise the bare `snapshot` group invocation; this is a latent defect against the stated contract ("a click group `snapshot` registered on monitor_cli"), not a regression. I was unable to apply the one-line reorder because tool execution was blocked mid-review.' additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 792, 'prompt_tokens': 71108, 'total_tokens': 71900, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 70912}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 70912, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 196}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-flash', 'system_fingerprint': 'bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6', 'id': '2ee47bd0-dec4-4435-9659-459bd0a7f77e', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None} id='lc_run--01a213d2-2c6f-7ab1-b145-187f9009c665-0' tool_calls=[] invalid_tool_calls=[] usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 71108, 'output_tokens': 792, 'total_tokens': 71900, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 70912}, 'output_token_details': {}}
