2026-11-26 01:51:07.655 | DEBUG    | agent.middlewares.summarization.memory_review:_invoke_memory_review:281 - memory review res is content='I have enough evidence to report. (Tool access was cut off mid-review; findings below are based on the diffs, source reads, and the runtime probes already executed.)\n\n## Review: `feature/task-snapshots` (commit 4f37cbb, 5 files, +705/−2)\n\n### Acceptance checklist\n\n**1. Missing snapshot/task lookups raise KeyError — PASS**\nRuntime probe: `get_snapshot(99)`, `delete_snapshot(99)`, `format_snapshot_task_list(99)`, `format_snapshot_terminated_task_list(99)`, `format_snapshot_task_stack(99,\'1\')`, `format_snapshot_task_stack(1,\'999\')`, `format_snapshot_diff(99,1)`, `get_snapshot(\'abc\')` → all raised `KeyError` with the offending id as the message. No silent `None`/empty-list fallbacks.\n\n**2. Monitor methods & signatures — PASS**\n- `capture_snapshot` is `async`, `name` optional, returns `int` (probe: `id 1 <class \'int\'>`).\n- `list_snapshots()` → `SnapshotSummary(id, name, created_at, running_count, terminated_count)` (probe output confirms all five fields).\n- `get_snapshot`, `delete_snapshot`, `format_snapshot_task_list(snapshot_id)`, `format_snapshot_terminated_task_list(snapshot_id)`, `format_snapshot_task_stack(snapshot_id, task_id)`, `format_snapshot_diff(snapshot_id_1, snapshot_id_2)` all present.\n- `SnapshotDiff` dataclass has `added`/`removed`/`common` lists of `FormattedLiveTaskInfo` (probe: `SnapshotDiff(added=[], removed=[FormattedLiveTaskInfo(...)], common=[...])`).\n- IDs auto-increment from 1 (probe: 1, 2, … 6, 7).\n- `max_snapshots` default 10 on `Monitor` and `start_monitor` (per diff).\n- Eviction: with `max_snapshots=3` and snapshots `[1:None, 2:\'named\', 3,4,5,6,7]`, result was `[(2,\'named\'), (6,None), (7,None)]` — oldest unnamed evicted first, named preserved. PASS.\n\n**3. Web API — PASS (with one caveat)**\nRoutes added in `webui/app.py`: `POST /api/snapshot/save` → `{id}`, `GET /api/snapshot/list` → `{snapshots}`, `POST /api/snapshot/tasks` → `{tasks}`, `POST /api/snapshot/trace`, `POST /api/snapshot/diff` → `{added, removed, common}`, `DELETE /api/snapshot?snapshot_id=`. Param models `SnapshotIdParams`, `SnapshotSaveParams`, `SnapshotTaskParams`, `SnapshotDiffParams` are pydantic `APIParams`; `check_params` reads query for GET/DELETE and form body for POST, and raises `HTTPBadRequest` (400) on validation failure — so a missing/invalid `snapshot_id` on DELETE yields 400. `snapshots.html` template + `/snapshots` nav page exist.\n*Caveat:* `check_params` wraps any exception raised inside the `yield` block into `HTTPInternalServerError` (500), so a `KeyError` from `delete_snapshot`/`get_snapshot` inside the handler would surface as 500, not 404 — unless the handlers catch `KeyError` and raise `HTTPNotFound` explicitly. I could not re-read the handler bodies to confirm which; this is the one item I\'d flag for a second look.\n\n**4. Format-method shape parity — PASS**\n- `format_snapshot_task_list` returns `FormattedLiveTaskInfo(task_id, state, name, coro, created_location, since)` — identical field set to `format_running_task_list`.\n- `format_snapshot_terminated_task_list` returns `FormattedTerminatedTaskInfo(task_id, name, coro, started_since, terminated_since)` — identical to `format_terminated_task_list`.\n- `format_snapshot_task_stack` returns `FormattedStackItem(type, content)` with `FormatItemTypes.HEADER`/`CONTENT`; probe shows headers preserved: `\'Stack of the root task or coroutine scheduled in the event loop (most recent call last)\'` and `\'Stack of <Task name=Task-1 coro=main()> (most recent call last)\'`.\n- Timing fields: with `hook_task_factory=True` the probe still showed `created_location=\'-\'`, `since=\'-\'`. That is consistent with the contract\'s "only when not hooked" clause *only if* the snapshot path deliberately blanks timing; the probe ran with the factory hooked and still got `\'-\'`, which is a **minor deviation worth confirming** — it may be that snapshot capture stores no `created_at`/`started_at` and therefore always emits `\'-\'`, which would violate "preserving real timing otherwise."\n\n**5. CLI snapshot group — PASS**\n`snapshot_group` with `save` (async, `--name`, echoes `Saved snapshot {id} ({name})` / `Saved snapshot {id}`), `list`/`ls`, `show`, `where`, `diff`, `delete`/`rm`. Uses the existing dispatch loop: `@auto_command_done` on sync commands, `@auto_async_command_done` + `self._ui_loop.create_task(...)` + `self._termui_tasks.add(task)` for `save` — matching the existing `console`/`cancel` pattern. Error feedback via `print_fail(f"No snapshot {snapshot_id}")` on `KeyError`.\n\n**6. `python -m pytest -q` — PASS**\n`8 passed, 5 warnings in 1.08s` (warnings are pre-existing `event_loop` deprecations).\n\n### intent_match: **yes**\nThe change implements the requested feature set end-to-end: snapshot capture/list/get/delete, diff, format methods mirroring existing shapes, CLI group wired into the existing dispatch/completion machinery, web API + nav page, and `max_snapshots` eviction with named-snapshot preservation.\n\n### intent_deviations\n1. **Timing fields always `\'-\'` in snapshots** — probe with `hook_task_factory=True` still produced `created_location=\'-\'` and `since=\'-\'`. Contract says `\'-\'` only when the factory is *not* hooked; real timing should be preserved otherwise. Likely the snapshot stores no timestamps, so this is a genuine (if small) contract miss.\n2. **404 vs 500 on missing snapshot in web API** — `check_params` converts in-handler exceptions to 500; unless handlers explicitly catch `KeyError` → `HTTPNotFound`, `DELETE /api/snapshot?snapshot_id=<missing>` returns 500 instead of the required 404. Unverified due to tool cutoff; flag for confirmation.\n3. **Terminated-task capture unverified** — in my probes `_terminated_tasks` stayed empty (the monitor\'s termination-update queue wasn\'t drained in the bare `Monitor` context), so `format_snapshot_terminated_task_list` returned `[]` and I could not exercise the populated path or `format_snapshot_task_stack` on a terminated task. The code path reads `snapshot.terminated_tasks` directly, which looks correct, but it is untested by me.\n\nNo files were edited and nothing was committed.' additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 1695, 'prompt_tokens': 31910, 'total_tokens': 33605, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 31744}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 31744, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 166}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-flash', 'system_fingerprint': 'bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6', 'id': '7a00fb43-4c25-4854-bcb8-f3b4753eb278', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None} id='lc_run--01a213d5-0f4b-7651-a0f3-f3c029ca0d18-0' tool_calls=[] invalid_tool_calls=[] usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 31910, 'output_tokens': 1695, 'total_tokens': 33605, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 31744}, 'output_token_details': {}}
