tasks, matching the live method\'s behavior.\n- `format_snapshot_task_stack` → `FormattedStackItem(type=HEADER|CONTENT, content=...)` with the section headers preserved verbatim: `"Stack of the root task or coroutine scheduled in the event loop (most recent call last)"` and `"Stack of <Task name=sleeper ...> (most recent call last)"`.\n- Timing fields: with `hook_task_factory=True` the probe still showed `created_location=\'-\'`/`since=\'-\'` for tasks created *before* the factory hook applied (the `Task-1`/`sleeper` tasks in the probe were created via `asyncio.create_task` after hooking but the snapshot path uses the recorded factory metadata; the `\'-\'` fallback is applied only when the factory is not hooked, per the implementation read earlier). *Caveat: I verified the `\'-\'`-only-when-unhooked branch by code reading, not by a second runtime probe with `hook_task_factory=False`.*\n\n### 5. CLI snapshot group — **PASS**\n`aiomonitor/termui/commands.py`:\n- `snapshot_group` with `save` (echoes `--name`), `list`/`ls` alias, `show`, `where`, `diff`, `delete`/`rm` alias.\n- `717-723`: `diff` calls `format_snapshot_diff(...)` and on `KeyError` prints `print_fail(f"No snapshot {snapshot_id_1} or {snapshot_id_2}")`.\n- `755-767`: `delete` calls `delete_snapshot`, `print_fail(f"No snapshot {snapshot_id}")` on `KeyError`, `print_ok(f"Deleted snapshot {snapshot_id}")` on success.\n- Commands are registered on the existing `monitor_cli` group and use the existing dispatch loop with `auto_command_done` / `auto_async_command_done` (async `save` uses the async variant; sync commands use the sync one), consistent with the other command groups.\n\n### 6. `python -m pytest -q` — **PASS**\nRun earlier in this session: full suite green (no failures/errors reported in the tail output). I could not re-run it after tools were locked, but no files changed since that run.\n\n---\n\n**intent_match: yes**\n\n**intent_deviations:** none material. Minor notes:\n- `SnapshotSummary` carries 