2026-11-26 01:54:45.141 | DEBUG    | agent.middlewares.summarization.memory_review:_invoke_memory_review:281 - memory review res is content='I\'ve been switched to a read-only background review, so I can\'t run further commands. Here is the completed report from the evidence already gathered.\n\n## Review Report — branch `feature/task-snapshots` (commit `4f37cbb`)\n\nScope: 5 files, +705/−2 (`aiomonitor/monitor.py`, `aiomonitor/termui/commands.py`, `aiomonitor/types.py`, `aiomonitor/webui/app.py`, `aiomonitor/webui/templates/snapshots.html`).\n\n### Item 5 — CLI snapshot group — **PASS**\n\n**Registered under the existing `monitor_cli` dispatch loop.** The interactive loop builds `command_done_event = asyncio.Event()` and a `command_done` contextvar token, then calls `ctx.run(monitor_cli.main, args, prog_name="", obj=self, standalone_mode=False, ...)` and `await command_done_event.wait()` (`commands.py:128-144`). The snapshot group is a normal sub-group of that same `monitor_cli` object — `@monitor_cli.group(name="snapshot", cls=AliasGroupMixin, add_help_option=False)` with `@click.pass_context`, `@custom_help_option`, `@auto_command_done` (`commands.py:608-616`) — so it is dispatched by the identical loop, no parallel path.\n\n**Completion signaling.** `auto_command_done` sets the event in a `finally` block; `auto_async_command_done` clears then sets it around the awaited coroutine (`commands.py:241-263`). `save` is the only async subcommand: its body is wrapped in `@auto_async_command_done` (`commands.py:626`) and scheduled on `self._ui_loop` while being tracked in `self._termui_tasks` (`commands.py:646-647`), matching the existing `cancel`/`console` pattern. `list`/`ls`, `show`, `where`, `diff`, `delete`/`rm` each carry `@auto_command_done` (`commands.py:652`, `679`, `697`, `713`, `758`).\n\n**`save --name` echoed.** `@click.option("-n", "--name", ...)` (`commands.py:619-621`); success path prints `print_ok(f"Saved snapshot {snapshot_id} ({name})")` when named, else `print_ok(f"Saved snapshot {snapshot_id}")` (`commands.py:641-644`).\n\n**Invalid IDs → `print_error`-style feedback, not a traceback.** Each handler catches `KeyError` locally and calls `print_fail` (the red `✗` printer, `commands.py:78-84`):\n- `show` — `except KeyError: print_fail(f"No snapshot {snapshot_id}")` (`commands.py:687`)\n- `where` — `except KeyError: print_fail(f"No task {task_id} in snapshot {snapshot_id}")` (`commands.py:704`)\n- `diff` — `except KeyError: print_fail(f"No snapshot {snapshot_id_1} or {snapshot_id_2}")` (`commands.py:723`)\n- `delete` — `except KeyError: print_fail(f"No snapshot {snapshot_id}")` (`commands.py:765`)\n- `save` — `except Exception as e: print_fail(repr(e))` (`commands.py:638-640`)\n\nBecause these are caught inside the command, the outer `except Exception: print_fail(traceback.format_exc())` (`commands.py:153-154`) is never reached for a bad ID — no traceback is shown.\n\n### Item 6 — `python -m pytest -q` — **PASS**\n`8 passed, 5 warnings in 1.08s`. No failures. Warnings are pre-existing `event_loop` fixture deprecations in `tests/test_monitor.py`.\n\n### PASS/FAIL table — contract items\n\n| # | Item | Verdict | Key evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Missing snapshot/task lookups raise `KeyError` | **PASS** | `monitor.py:603-611` (`get_snapshot`), `613-621` (`delete_snapshot`), `623-639` (both list formatters via `get_snapshot`), `641-657` (`format_snapshot_task_stack`, incl. `raise KeyError(task_id)`), `659-672` (`format_snapshot_diff`); `_normalize_snapshot_id` `monitor.py:525-529`. Probe: all 8 cases raised `KeyError`, zero `NO RAISE`. |\n| 2 | Monitor methods/signatures, IDs from 1, `max_snapshots=10`, eviction | **PASS** | `capture_snapshot` async, `name=None`, returns int — `monitor.py:543-586`; `list_snapshots` — `588-601`; `SnapshotSummary` fields `types.py:83-93`; `SnapshotDiff` `types.py:96-104`; `_next_snapshot_id = 1` `monitor.py:168`, increment `572-573`; `max_snapshots: int = 10` `monitor.py:129` and `808` (forwarded `840`); eviction `531-541`. Probe: ids `1, 2`; after 7 captures with cap 3 → `[(2,\'named\'), (6,None), (7,None)]`. |\n| 3 | Web API + `/snapshots` page | **PASS** | Routes `app.py:421-426`; `save`→`{"id"}` `262-266`; `list`→`{"snapshots"}` `269-285`; `tasks`→`{"tasks"}` `288-313`; `trace` `316-343`; `diff`→`{"added","removed","common"}` `346-384`; `delete` query param `387-399`; 404 on `KeyError`, 400 via `check_params` (`webui/utils.py:29-40`); nav `app.py:78-81`, route `412`, handler `159-169`, template `snapshots.html`. |\n| 4 | Format-shape parity, `\'-\'` only when unhooked, headers preserved | **PASS** | Snapshot lists store the exact objects from `format_running_task_list`/`format_terminated_task_list` (`monitor.py:548-549`, `578-579`) and return them verbatim (`630`, `639`); `\'-\'` logic inherited from `monitor.py:266-282`; stacks stored from `format_running_task_stack`/`format_terminated_task_stack` (`347-429`, `431-512`) with `FormatItemTypes.HEADER` intact (probe showed both root and task headers). |\n| 5 | CLI snapshot group | **PASS** | See detail above — `commands.py:128-144`, `241-263`, `608-767`. |\n| 6 | `python -m pytest -q` | **PASS** | `8 passed, 5 warnings in 1.08s`. |\n\n### PASS/FAIL table — acceptance checklist\n\n| # | Item | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | All missing snapshot and task lookups raise `KeyError` | **PASS** |\n| 2 | Monitor methods with required signatures; `list_snapshots` summaries carry `id, name, running_count, terminated_count`; diff object has `added/removed/common` | **PASS** |\n| 3 | `/api/snapshot/` JSON: save(POST→`{id}`), list(GET→`{snapshots}`), tasks(POST `snapshot_id`→`{tasks}`), trace(POST `snapshot_id`+`task_id`), diff(POST `snapshot_id_1`+`snapshot_id_2`→`{added,removed,common}`) | **PASS** |\n| 4 | Snapshot formatters match existing attribute shapes; `\'-\'` only when factory unhooked; stack headers preserved | **PASS** |\n\n### intent_match: **yes**\n\n### intent_deviations\nNo material deviations. Items worth flagging:\n\n1. **Trace endpoint response shape** — `POST /api/snapshot/trace` returns `{"trace": [...]}` (`app.py:316-343`), not a bare list. The contract only names the endpoint, so this is an unspecified choice; it is consistent with the sibling endpoints\' envelope style.\n2. **Extra aliases** — `list` also answers to `ls` and `delete` to `rm` (`commands.py:650`, `755`). Additive beyond the contract; no behavior removed.\n3. **`\'-\'` timing semantics** — `\'-\'` is emitted when the task factory is not hooked *or* the task is a root task with no creation traceback (`monitor.py:266-282`). This is inherited verbatim from the pre-existing formatters rather than newly introduced, so snapshot output matches live output exactly; strictly it is slightly broader than "only when not hooked."\n4. **Eviction fallback** — when every snapshot is named, the oldest *named* snapshot is evicted (`monitor.py:531-541`) to keep memory bounded. A reasonable reading of "preserving named," but not spelled out in the contract.\n5. **`is_root` derivation** — `created_location == "-"` (`app.py:308`, `373`) is also true for an unhooked factory; mirrors existing `/api/live-tasks` (`app.py:213`).\n6. **Dead field** — `Snapshot.running_task_ids` is populated (`monitor.py:582`) but never read; `format_snapshot_diff` recomputes keys from `running_tasks` (`667-668`). Harmless.\n7. **Duplication** — `_print_stack_items` / `_print_live_task_table` / `_print_terminated_task_table` (`commands.py:537-605`) copy the bodies of `do_where`/`do_ps`/`do_ps_terminated` instead of refactoring them. No behavior change.\n8. **No new tests** — the suite remains 8 tests; the contract only required it to pass, which it does.\n\n**Test status: pass**' additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 2299, 'prompt_tokens': 49865, 'total_tokens': 52164, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens'