ls"]` — `commands.py:650`; `show` — `676`; `where` — `693`; `diff` — `709`; `delete` with `aliases=["rm"]` — `755`. Aliases resolve through `AliasGroupMixin.get_command` (`commands.py:200-205`).\n\n**Invalid-ID feedback instead of an unhandled `KeyError`**\n- `show` — `commands.py:679-690`: `try: ... self.format_snapshot_task_list(snapshot_id) ... except KeyError: print_fail(f"No snapshot {snapshot_id}"); return` (687).\n- `where` — `commands.py:693-706`: `try: ... self.format_snapshot_task_stack(snapshot_id, task_id) ... except KeyError: print_fail(f"No task {task_id} in snapshot {snapshot_id}"); return` (704).\n- `diff` — `commands.py:709-752`: `try: ... self.format_snapshot_diff(snapshot_id_1, snapshot_id_2) ... except KeyError: print_fail(f"No snapshot {snapshot_id_1} or {snapshot_id_2}"); return` (723).\n- `delete` — `commands.py:755-767`: `try: self.delete_snapshot(snapshot_id) except KeyError: print_fail(f"No snapshot {snapshot_id}"); return` (763-765).\n- `save` — `commands.py:634-640`: broad `except Exception as e: print_fail(repr(e)); return`, so a capture failure also surfaces as feedback rather than a traceback.\n- `print_fail` is the existing red-failure printer (`commands.py:67-84`), so output styling matches the rest of the CLI.\n\n**Item 5: PASS**\n\n## Item 6 — `python -m pytest -q`\n\n`8 passed, 5 warnings in 1.08s` (warnings are pre-existing `event_loop` fixture deprecations in `tests/test_monitor.py`). No failures, no errors, no failure names to report.\n\n**Item 6: PASS**\n\n## PASS/FAIL table — contract items 1-6\n\n| # | Contract item | Result | Key evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Missing snapshot/task lookups raise `KeyError` | **PASS** | `monitor.py:603-611` (get), `613-621` (delete), `623-639` (both lists via `get_snapshot`), `641-657` (stack: snapshot + `raise KeyError(task_id)`), `659-672` (diff); probe raised `KeyError` in all 8 cases, no `NO RAISE` |\n| 2 | Monitor methods/signatures, IDs from 1, `max_snapshots=10`, eviction | **PASS** | `monitor.py:543-586` async `capture_snapshot(name=None)->int`; `588-601` `list_snapshots`; `603-621`; `623-672`; `types.py:83-104`; `_next_snapshot_id=1` at `168`; `max_snapshots=10` at `129` and `808`; eviction `531-541`; probe `ids 1 2`, `after evict [(2,\'named\'),(6,None),(7,None)]` |\n| 3 | Web API endpoints + `/snapshots` page | **PASS** | `app.py:421-426` routes; `262-266` save→`{id}`; `269-285` list→`{snapshots}`; `288-313` tasks→`{tasks}`; `316-343` trace; `346-384` diff→`{added,removed,common}`; `387-399` delete; 404s at `293-297/323-332/353-362/392-396`; 400 via `webui/utils.py:29-40`; nav `app.py:78-81`, route `412`, handler `159-169`, template `snapshots.html` |\n| 4 | Format-shape parity, `\'-\'` only when unhooked, headers preserved | **PASS** | capture stores the exact objects from `format_running_task_list`/`format_terminated_task_list` (`monitor.py:548-549`, `578-579`); `\'-\'` logic inherited from `266-282`; stack items from `347-429`/`431-512` incl. `FormatItemTypes.HEADER`; probe showed real frames when hooked, `\'-\'` when not |\n| 5 | CLI snapshot group + dispatch loop + signaling + error feedback | **PASS** | `commands.py:608-616` group; `619-647` save (`--name` echoed `641-644`, `auto_async_command_done` `626`); `650` list/ls; `676` show; `693` where; `709` diff; `755` delete/rm; loop `128-144`; decorators `241-250`/`253-263`; `except KeyError → print_fail` at `687`, `704`, `723`, `763-765` |\n| 6 | `python -m pytest -q` passes | **PASS** | `8 passed, 5 warnings in 1.08s` |\n\n## PASS/FAIL table — acceptance checklist items 1-4\n\n| # | Checklist item | Result | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | All missing snapshot and task lookups raise `KeyError` | **PASS** | `monitor.py:603-611`, `613-621`, `623-639`, `641-657`, `659-672`; probe: 8/8 `KeyError` |\n| 2 | Monitor methods with exact signatures; diff object with `added`/`removed`/`common` | **PASS** | `monitor.py:543-586`, `588-601`, `603-621`, `623-630`, `632-639`, `641-657`, `659-672`; `SnapshotDiff` at `types.py:96-104`; probe `SnapshotDiff(added=[], removed=[...], common=[...])` |\n| 3 | Web API JSON at `/api/snapshot/` (save/list/tasks/trace/diff) | **PASS** | `app.py:262-266`, `269-285`, `288-313`, `316-343`, `346-384`, routes `421-426` |\n| 4 | Format methods match existing shapes; `\'-\'` only when factory unhooked; headers preserved | **PASS** | `monitor.py:548-549`, `578-579`, `266-282`, `347-429`, `431-512`; probe output with real frames + `HEADER` items |\n\n## intent_match: **yes**\n\n## intent_deviations\n\nNo material deviations. Items that diverge from a literal reading of the contract, or that go beyond it:\n\n1. **Trace endpoint response shape** — `POST /api/snapshot/trace` returns `{"trace": [...]}` (`app.py:316-343`), not a bare list. The contract only specified the request (`snapshot_id` + `task_id`), so this is an unspecified choice; it is consistent with the existing `/api/stack-trace` shape.\n2. **Extra aliases** — `list` also answers to `ls` (`commands.py:650`) and `delete` to `rm` (`commands.py:755`). The contract named only `list`/`delete`; the aliases are additive and resolved by the existing `AliasGroupMixin` (`commands.py:200-205`).\n3. **`\'-\'` timing semantics** — `\'-\'` is emitted when the task factory is not hooked *or* when the task is a root task with no recorded creation traceback (`monitor.py:266-282`). This is inherited verbatim from the pre-existing `format_running_task_list`, so snapshot output matches live output exactly; it is slightly broader than "only when the factory is not hooked".\n4. **Eviction fallback** — when every snapshot is named, eviction drops the oldest *named* snapshot (`monitor.py:531-541`) to keep memory bounded. The contract said "preserving named" without specifying this all-named case.\n5. **400 vs 404 split** — missing/blank required params yield 400 via `check_params` (`webui/utils.py:29-40`), while well-formed but unknown IDs yield 404 (`app.py:293-297`, `323-332`, `353-362`, `392-396`). This matches the contract\'s "404 when missing and 400 when param invalid" reading, but note the wording is ambiguous and the implementation chose param-validation→400, unknown-ID→404.\n6. **Dead field** — `Snapshot.running_task_ids` is populated (`monitor.py:582`) but never read; `format_snapshot_diff` recomputes keys from `running_tasks` (`monitor.py:667-668`). Harmless.\n7. **`is_root` heuristic** — `app.py:308,373` derives `is_root` from `created_location == "-"`, which is also true when the factory is merely unhooked; mirrors existing `/api/live-tasks` (`app.py:213`).\n8. **Duplicated printers** — `_print_stack_items` / `_print_live_task_table` / `_print_terminated_task_table` (`commands.py:537-605`) duplicate `do_where`/`do_ps`/`do_ps_terminated` bodies rather than refactoring them; duplication only, no behavior change.\n9. **No new tests** — the suite remains 8 tests; the contract only required it to pass, which it does.\n\n**Test status: pass** — read-only review; no files edited, nothing committed.' additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 2715, 'prompt_tokens': 50651, 'total_tokens': 53366, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 50432}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 50432, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 219}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-flash', 'system_fingerprint': 'bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6', 'id': '91f89b03-835d-4b45-bcff-5ecbf560c418', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None} id='lc_run--01a213d8-950d-7421-b542-b98dcc6418c0-0' tool_calls=[] invalid_tool_calls=[] usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 50651, 'output_tokens': 2715, 'total_tokens': 53366, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 50432}, 'output_token_details': {}}
