2026-11-26 02:09:26.317 | DEBUG    | agent.middlewares.summarization.memory_review:_invoke_memory_review:281 - memory review res is content='# packages/core Reconnaissance Report — Snapshot / Rollback Feature\n\nAll paths are relative to `packages/core/`. Line numbers are from the current working tree. **No files were modified during this reconnaissance.**\n\n> **Working-tree state (important):** an *uncommitted, untracked* draft already exists at `src/snapshot/snapshot.ts` (19,991 bytes, 585 lines) plus edits to `src/index.ts`, `src/world/world.ts`, `src/world/types.ts`, `src/entity/types.ts`, `src/entity/entity-methods-patch.ts`. `git status` also shows stray scratch files `packages/core/dbg.ts` and `packages/core/scratch-snapshot.ts`.\n>\n> **Missing files:** `src/snapshot/index.ts` does **not** exist (only `src/snapshot/snapshot.ts`), and `tests/snapshot.test.ts` does **not** exist.\n\n---\n\n## (d) Trait system — first, because it gates the registry design\n\n### d.1 Trait creation: id, schema, storage type\n\n`src/trait/trait.ts:47-90`\n```ts\nconst tagSchema = Object.freeze({});\nlet traitId = 0;                                   // module-global monotonic counter\n\nfunction createTrait<S extends Schema>(schema: S = tagSchema as S): Trait<Norm<S>> {\n    const isAoS = typeof schema === \'function\';\n    const isTag = !isAoS && Object.keys(schema).length === 0;\n    const traitType: StoreType = isAoS ? \'aos\' : isTag ? \'tag\' : \'soa\';\n    validateSchema(schema);\n    const id = traitId++;\n    const Trait = Object.assign((params) => [Trait, params], {\n        [$internal]: { id, set, fastSet, fastSetWithChangeDetection, get,\n                       createStore: () => createStore<S>(schema), relation: null, type: traitType },\n    });\n    Object.defineProperty(Trait, \'id\',     { value: id,     writable: false, enumerable: true });\n    Object.defineProperty(Trait, \'schema\', { value: schema, writable: false, enumerable: true });\n    return Trait;\n}\nexport const trait = createTrait;\n```\n\n- **`trait.id`** — process-global integer (`traitId++`), *not* per-world; it is the index into `world[$internal].traitInstances`.\n- **`trait.schema`** — the raw schema: plain object (SoA), factory function (AoS), or `{}` (tag).\n- **`trait[$internal].type`** — `\'soa\' | \'aos\' | \'tag\'`, the discriminator a registry must capture.\n- **`trait[$internal].relation`** — `null` for plain traits, the owning `Relation` for relation-backed traits.\n- Traits are **functions** (callable to produce `[Trait, params]` tuples) and carry **no name**, so identity comparison (`===`) is the only safe key.\n\n### d.2 Default values\n\n`src/storage/schema.ts:7-26`\n```ts\nexport function getSchemaDefaults(schema, type): Record<string, any> | null {\n    if (type === \'aos\') return typeof schema === \'function\' ? schema() : null;\n    if (!schema || typeof schema === \'function\' || Object.keys(schema).length === 0) return null;\n    const defaults = {};\n    for (const key in schema) defaults[key] = typeof schema[key] === \'function\' ? schema[key]() : schema[key];\n    return defaults;\n}\n```\nDefaults are applied inside `addTrait` (`src/trait/trait.ts:159-169`): AoS → `params ?? defaults`; SoA → `{...defaults, ...params}`; tag → nothing. **Rollback must not rely on `addTrait` defaults** — it must `addTrait` then `setTrait(..., false)` with the snapshot value (the draft does exactly this).\n\n### d.3 Per-entity storage layout — plain JS arrays, NOT typed arrays\n\n`src/storage/stores.ts:4-17`\n```ts\nexport function createStore(schema) {\n    if (typeof schema === \'function\') return [];              // AoS: one slot per entity id\n    const store = {};\n    for (const key in schema) store[key] = [];                // SoA: one array per property\n    return store;\n}\n```\n`src/storage/types.ts:6-18`\n```ts\nexport type Store<T> = T extends AoSFactory ? ReturnType<T>[]\n    : { [P in keyof T]: ...[] };\nexport type StoreType = \'aos\' | \'soa\' | \'tag\';\n```\n- **SoA**: `store = { x: number[], y: number[] }`, indexed by **entity id** (`getEntityId(entity)`), not by dense index.\n- **AoS**: `store = unknown[]`, `store[eid]` is the instance object.\n- **Tag**: no data at all (accessors are no-ops).\n- Stores are **plain `Array`s** — see the comment at `src/world/utils/increment-world-bit-flag.ts:4-5` explaining native arrays are used deliberately to avoid overflow on recycling.\n- Stores live on the per-world `TraitInstance`: `src/trait/types.ts:84-106` (`store: Store<S>`, `schema`, `bitflag`, `generationId`, `relationTargets?`).\n\n### d.4 Registration per world\n\n`src/trait/trait.ts:94-125`\n```ts\nexport function registerTrait(world: World, trait: Trait) {\n    const ctx = world[$internal];\n    const data: TraitInstance = {\n        generationId: ctx.entityMasks.length - 1,\n        bitflag: ctx.bitflag,\n        trait,\n        store: traitCtx.createStore(),\n        queries: new Set(), trackingQueries: new Set(), notQueries: new Set(),\n        relationQueries: new Set(),\n        schema: trait.schema,\n        changeSubscriptions: new Set(), addSubscriptions: new Set(), removeSubscriptions: new Set(),\n    };\n    setTraitInstance(ctx.traitInstances, trait, data);   // traitInstances[trait.id] = data\n    world.traits.add(trait);\n    if (traitCtx.relation) ctx.relations.add(traitCtx.relation);\n    incrementWorldBitflag(world);\n    if (isOrderedTrait(trait)) setupOrderedTraitSync(world, trait);\n}\n```\n`src/trait/trait-instance.ts:8-40` — `getTraitInstance(arr, trait) => arr[trait.id]`, `hasTraitInstance`, `setTraitInstance` (grows the array to `id + 1`).\n\n### d.5 Read / write a single trait value for one entity\n\n**Read** — `src/trait/trait.ts:373-381`\n```ts\nfunction getTraitForTrait(world, entity, trait) {\n    if (!hasTrait(world, entity, trait)) return undefined;\n    const store = getStore(world, trait);\n    return trait[$internal].get(getEntityId(entity), store);   // SoA: builds {x,y}; AoS: store[eid]\n}\n```\n**Write** — `src/trait/trait.ts:406-422`\n```ts\nfunction setTraitForTrait(world, entity, trait, value, triggerChanged) {\n    const ctx = trait[$internal];\n    const store = getStore(world, trait);\n    const index = getEntityId(entity);\n    value instanceof Function && (value = value(ctx.get(index, store)));\n    ctx.set(index, store, value);\n    triggerChanged && setChanged(world, entity, trait);\n}\n```\nPublic wrappers: `getTrait(world, entity, trait|pair)` (`:351`), `setTrait(world, entity, trait|pair, value, triggerChanged = true)` (`:340`), `hasTrait` (`:319`), `getStore` (`:331`).\n\n**Presence check is a bitmask test, not a store lookup** — `src/trait/trait.ts:319-329`\n```ts\nexport function hasTrait(world, entity, trait) {\n    const instance = getTraitInstance(ctx.traitInstances, trait);\n    if (!instance) return false;\n    const { generationId, bitflag } = instance;\n    return (ctx.entityMasks[generationId][getEntityId(entity)] & bitflag) === bitflag;\n}\n```\n\n**Accessor generation** — `src/storage/accessors.ts:3-137`: SoA set/get are `new Function`-generated per schema key (`store.${key}[index] = value.${key}` / `{ key: store.key[index] }`); AoS set/get are `store[index] = value` / `store[index]`; tag accessors are `noop`.\n\n### d.6 Relations (also trait-backed) — completed\n\n`src/relation/relation.ts:18-87` — `relation({ exclusive, autoDestroy, store })` creates an **underlying trait** (`trait(definition?.store ?? {})`) and then sets `traitCtx.relation = relation` on that trait\'s `$internal`. So a relation *is* a trait with a non-null `relation` back-pointer; the relation\'s own data store is the trait\'s store.\n\nTargets are held on the `TraitInstance`, not in the store — `src/relation/types.ts:19-26`, `src/trait/types.ts:100-105`:\n```ts\nrelationTargets?: number[] | number[][];   // number[] for exclusive, number[][] otherwise\n```\n\nRelation API surface:\n- `getRelationTargets(world, relation, entity)` — `relation.ts:95-115`\n- `addRelationTarget(world, relation, entity, target)` — `relation.ts:202-248` (returns target index, `-1` if no-op)\n- `removeRelationTarget(world, relation, entity, target)` — `relation.ts:254-304` (returns `{ removedIndex, wasLastTarget }`)\n- `getRelationData(world, relation, entity, target)` — `relation.ts:497-535`\n- `setRelationData(world, relation, entity, target, data)` — `relation.ts:482-492`\n- `setRelationDataAtIndex(world, relation, entity, index, data)` — `relation.ts:441-477`\n- `hasRelationPair(world, relation, entity, target)` — `relation.ts:540-555`\n- `isRelation(value)` — `src/relation/utils/is-relation.ts` (used by the draft to accept relations in registry entries)\n\n**Registry implication:** a relation must be registered under its own key and snapshotted as `{ targetId, data? }[]`; the underlying trait must **not** also be snapshotted as a plain trait. The draft skips it via `if (traitCtx.relation) { ... continue; }` when walking `entityTraits`.\n\n### d.7 What a trait registry must capture — summary\n\n| Requirement | Source of truth | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Trait identity** | the trait function itself, compared with `===` | traits have no name; `Map`/`Set` keying by the function is the only stable identity |\n| **`trait.id`** | `trait.id` (`trait.ts:60`) | index into `world[$internal].traitInstances`; needed to reach the store/bitflag |\n| **`trait.schema`** | `trait.schema` (`trait.ts:61`) | needed to know the property keys for SoA records and to re-create AoS instances |\n| **`$internal.type`** | `\'soa\' \\| \'aos\' \\| \'tag\'` (`trait.ts:56`) | tag ⇒ snapshot value is `true` and there is no data to read/write |\n| **Relation membership** | `$internal.relation !== null` | decides whether to snapshot as `{targetId, data?}[]` instead of a plain record |\n| **Store shape** | `createStore(schema)` (`stores.ts:4-17`) | SoA = per-key arrays indexed by entity id; AoS = single array of instances; tag = none |\n| **Registry key (string)** | supplied by the caller | the serialisable name used in `EntitySnapshot.traits` / `.relations` |\n\n---\n\n## (a) `src/index.ts` — export style and where a snapshot export belongs\n\nStyle: **flat named re-exports, one statement per module, no `export *` anywhere.** Value exports and type exports are separate statements; types use `export type { ... } from \'...\'`.\n\n`src/index.ts:1-5`\n```ts\nexport { createActions } from \'./actions/create-actions\';\nexport type { Actions, ActionsInitializer, ActionRecord } from \'./actions/types\';\nexport { $internal } from \'./common\';\nexport type { Entity } from \'./entity/types\';\nexport { unpackEntity } from \'./entity/utils/pack-entity\';\n```\n\nThe draft already inserted the snapshot block between `relation` and `ordered`:\n\n`src/index.ts:29-46`\n```ts\nexport { relation } from \'./relation/relation\';\nexport {\n    createTraitRegistry,\n    diffEntitySnapshots,\n    diffWorldSnapshots,\n    rollbackEntity,\n    rollbackWorld,\n    snapshotEntity,\n    snapshotWorld,\n} from \'./snapshot/snapshot\';\nexport type {\n    EntitySnapshot,\n    EntitySnapshotDiff,\n    RelationSnapshotEntry,\n    TraitRegistry,\n    WorldSnapshot,\n    WorldSnapshotDiff,\n} from \'./snapshot/snapshot\';\n```\n\n**Exact position for `export * from \'./snapshot/index.js\'`:** immediately after the `relation` export line and before the `ordered`/`query` exports — i.e. at **`src/index.ts:30`**, in the alphabetical slot `actions → common → entity → ordered → query → relation → snapshot → storage → trait → universe → world`.\n\n**Caveat on the specifier:** the repo convention is **extensionless** (`\'./snapshot/snapshot\'`, `\'./relation/relation\'`, …). A `.js` suffix would be the only one in the package, and **`src/snapshot/index.ts` does not exist**, so `export * from \'./snapshot/index.js\'` would not resolve today. Two consistent options:\n1. Keep the single-file re-export `from \'./snapshot/snapshot\'` (matches every other module) — what the draft does.\n2. Add `src/snapshot/index.ts` re-exporting from `./snapshot`, then write `export * from \'./snapshot\'` (still extensionless).\n\n---\n\n## (b) `src/world/world.ts` — World shape, public methods, conventions\n\n`createWorld` is a **factory returning an object literal cast `as World`** (there is no `class World`), with read-only props added via `Object.defineProperty`.\n\n`src/world/world.ts:30-36`\n```ts\nexport function createWorld(options: WorldOptions): World;\nexport function createWorld(...traits: ConfigurableTrait[]): World;\nexport function createWorld(optionsOrFirstTrait?, ...traits): World {\n    const id = allocateWorldId(universe.worldIndex);\n```\n\nInternal state — `src/world/world.ts:59-80`\n```ts\nconst world = {\n    [$internal]: {\n        entityIndex: createEntityIndex(id),\n        entityMasks: [[]],          // number[][] — bitmask generations\n        entityTraits: new Map(),    // Map<Entity, Set<Trait>>\n        bitflag: 1,\n        traitInstances: [],         // (TraitInstance|undefined)[] indexed by trait.id\n        relations: new Set(),\n        queriesHashMap: new Map(), queryInstances: [], actionInstances: [],\n        notQueries: new Set(), dirtyQueries: new Set(), dirtyMasks: new Map(),\n        trackingSnapshots: new Map(), changedMasks: new Map(),\n        worldEntity: null!, trackedTraits: new Set(), resetSubscriptions: new Set(),\n    } as WorldInternal,\n    traits: new Set<Trait>(),\n```\n\nHow things are held:\n- **Traits** — `world.traits: Set<Trait>` (public) plus `ctx.traitInstances[trait.id]: TraitInstance` (store, bitflag, generationId, relationTargets).\n- **Entities** — `ctx.entityIndex` (dense/sparse/aliveCount/maxId), `ctx.entityMasks[generation][entityId]` bitmasks, `ctx.entityTraits: Map<Entity, Set<Trait>>`.\n- **Stores** — never on the world directly; always `getStore(world, trait)` → `ctx.traitInstances[trait.id].store`.\n\nPublic methods (all inline in the literal): `init` (`:82`), `spawn` (`:108`), `has` (`:112`), `add` (`:118`), `remove` (`:122`), `get` (`:126`), `set` (`:130`), `destroy` (`:134`), `reset` (`:146`), **`snapshot` (`:187`)**, **`rollback` (`:191`)**, `query` (`:195`), `queryFirst`, `onQueryAdd`, `onQueryRemove`, `onAdd`, `onRemove`, `onChange`.\n\nRepresentative snippet — `src/world/world.ts:187-193`\n```ts\nsnapshot(registry: TraitRegistry): WorldSnapshot {\n    return snapshotWorld(world, registry);\n},\n\nrollback(registry: TraitRegistry, checkpoint: WorldSnapshot) {\n    return rollbackWorld(world, registry, checkpoint);\n},\n```\n\nRead-only getters — `src/world/world.ts:387-399`\n```ts\nObject.defineProperty(world, \'id\',            { get: () => id, enumerable: true });\nObject.defineProperty(world, \'isInitialized\', { get: () => isInitialized, enumerable: true });\nObject.defineProperty(world, \'entities\',      { get: () => getAliveEntities(world[$internal].entityIndex), enumerable: true });\n```\n\nTyping conventions: `World` is a **type alias with method-signature syntax** (not a class) in `src/world/types.ts:49-127`; `WorldInternal` at `:29-47`. JSDoc is sparse — short `/** ... */` one-liners only on non-obvious fields (e.g. `src/world/types.ts:89-95`). New members are plain method signatures:\n\n`src/world/types.ts:64-67`\n```ts\ndestroy(): void;\nreset(): void;\nsnapshot(registry: TraitRegistry): WorldSnapshot;\nrollback(registry: TraitRegistry, checkpoint: WorldSnapshot): void;\n```\nwith `import type { TraitRegistry, WorldSnapshot } from \'../snapshot/snapshot\';` at `src/world/types.ts:13`.\n\n---\n\n## (c) `src/entity/entity-methods-patch.ts` — per-entity method attachment pattern\n\nEntities are **raw numbers**; convenience methods are monkey-patched onto `Number.prototype`, each guarded with `// @ts-expect-error` and a `this: Entity` annotation. The module is imported for side effects from `src/entity/entity.ts:11-12` (`import \'./entity-methods-patch\';`).\n\n`src/entity/entity-methods-patch.ts:1-4, 20-23`\n```ts\n// Add methods to the Number prototype so it can be used as an entity.\n// This lets us keep the performance of raw numbers over using objects\n// and the convenience of using methods. Type guards are used to ensure\n// that the methods are only called on entities.\n\n// @ts-expect-error\nNumber.prototype.add = function (this: Entity, ...traits: ConfigurableTrait[]) {\n    return addTrait(getEntityWorld(this), this, ...traits);\n};\n```\n\nThe draft\'s additions — `src/entity/entity-methods-patch.ts:89-101`\n```ts\n//@ts-expect-error\nNumber.prototype.snapshot = function (this: Entity, registry: TraitRegistry) {\n    return snapshotEntity(getEntityWorld(this), this, registry);\n};\n\n//@ts-expect-error\nNumber.prototype.rollback = function (\n    this: Entity,\n    registry: TraitRegistry,\n    snapshot: EntitySnapshot\n) {\n    return rollbackEntity(getEntityWorld(this), this, registry, snapshot);\n};\n```\n\n**Exact steps to add a new per-entity convenience method:**\n1. **Patch the prototype** at the bottom of `entity-methods-patch.ts`, resolving the world with `getEntityWorld(this)` and delegating to the free function. Prefix with `//@ts-expect-error` (note: the file uses both `// @ts-expect-error` and `//@ts-expect-error`; the newer additions use the no-space form).\n2. **Add the signature** to the `Entity` intersection type in `src/entity/types.ts:12-31`:\n   ```ts\n   export type Entity = number & {\n       add: (...traits: ConfigurableTrait[]) => void;\n       ...\n       isAlive: () => boolean;\n       snapshot: (registry: TraitRegistry) => EntitySnapshot;\n       rollback: (registry: TraitRegistry, snapshot: EntitySnapshot) => void;\n   };\n   ```\n   with `import type { EntitySnapshot, TraitRegistry } from \'../snapshot/snapshot\';` at `src/entity/types.ts:2`.\n3. **Import the implementation + types** at the top of the patch file (`src/entity/entity-methods-patch.ts:11-12`).\n\nExisting methods for reference: `add` `:21`, `remove` `:26`, `has` `:31`, `destroy` `:38`, `changed` `:43`, `get` `:48`, `set` `:53`, `targetsFor` `:63`, `targetFor` `:68`, `id` `:73`, `generation` `:78`, `isAlive` `:83`.\n\n---\n\n## (e) Entity creation / destruction and id recycling\n\n**Create** — `src/entity/entity.ts:14-29`\n```ts\nexport function createEntity(world: World, ...traits: ConfigurableTrait[]): Entity {\n    const ctx = world[$internal];\n    const entity = allocateEntity(ctx.entityIndex);\n    for (const query of ctx.notQueries) { ... }\n    ctx.entityTraits.set(entity, new Set());\n    addTrait(world, entity, ...traits);\n    return entity;\n}\n```\n\n**Allocation / recycling** — `src/entity/utils/entity-index.ts:41-59`\n```ts\nexport const allocateEntity = (index: EntityIndex): Entity => {\n    if (index.aliveCount < index.dense.length) {\n        // Recycle entity\n        const recycledEntity = incrementGeneration(index.dense[index.aliveCount]);\n        index.dense[index.aliveCount] = recycledEntity;\n        index.sparse[getEntityId(recycledEntity)] = index.aliveCount;\n        index.aliveCount++;\n        return recycledEntity;\n    }\n    const id = index.maxId++;\n    const entity = packEntity(index.worldId, 0, id);\n    index.dense.push(entity);\n    index.sparse[id] = index.aliveCount;\n    index.aliveCount++;\n    return entity;\n};\n```\n**IDs ARE recycled** (from the dense tail) and the **generation counter is bumped** on reuse (`incrementGeneration`, `src/entity/utils/pack-entity.ts:42-45`). Packing layout: `worldId:4 | generation:8 | entityId:20` (`pack-entity.ts:4-16`).\n\n**Destroy** — `src/entity/entity.ts:34-111`: validates liveness (`throw new Error(\'Koota: The entity being destroyed does not exist.\')`), cascades relation cleanup per `autoDestroy`, removes all traits, `releaseEntity` (swap-and-pop, `entity-index.ts:66-82`), removes from the all-query, deletes `entityTraits`, zeroes bitmasks.\n\n**Implications for rolling back destroyed entities:**\n- A destroyed entity\'s *packed* value is gone and its id may be handed out again with a **higher generation**, so a snapshot must store the **bare `entityId`** (`getEntityId(entity)`), never the packed value.\n- Rollback must **re-materialise** the entity: pack with `generation = 0` and repair `dense`/`sparse`/`aliveCount`/`maxId`/`entityTraits`/all-query. The draft does this in `ensureEntityWithId` (`src/snapshot/snapshot.ts:380-408`).\n- Consequence: re-created entities have generation `0`, so a stale pre-rollback handle with a higher generation correctly reports `isAlive() === false` — desirable, but must be documented.\n- Because ids are recycled, `rollbackWorld` must destroy **all** non-world entities first (so the dense/sparse arrays are consistent) before re-creating by id.\n\n---\n\n## (f) `package.json` scripts and test layout / import conventions\n\n`packages/core/package.json`\n```json\n{\n  "name": "@koota/core", "private": true, "type": "module",\n  "main": "./src/index.ts", "types": "./src/index.ts",\n  "scripts": { "test": "vitest", "lint": "oxlint" },\n  "devDependencies": { "@config/oxlint": "workspace:*", "@config/typescript": "workspace:*", "vitest": "catalog:" }\n}\n```\nRoot `/package.json`: `test` → `pnpm -F core test run && pnpm -F react test run`; `lint` → `pnpm -r lint`; `format` → prettier with `.config/prettier/base.json`.\n\n**Test runner:** Vitest, ESM (`"type": "module"`), **no globals** — every test imports `describe`/`it`/`expect`/`beforeEach`/`vi` explicitly from `\'vitest\'`.\n\n**Layout:** flat `tests/*.test.ts` — `actions`, `entity`, `ordered`, `query-modifiers`, `query`, `relation`, `trait`, `world` — plus `tests/utils/sparse-set.test.ts`. **No `tests/snapshot.test.ts` exists yet.**\n\n**Import conventions** (`tests/trait.test.ts:1-2`, `tests/world.test.ts:1-2`, `tests/entity.test.ts:1-2`, `tests/relation.test.ts:1-2`):\n```ts\nimport { beforeEach, describe, expect, it, vi } from \'vitest\';\nimport { createWorld, type Entity, getStore, trait } from \'../src\';\n```\n```ts\nimport { beforeEach, describe, expect, it } from \'vitest\';\nimport { createWorld, relation, type TraitRecord, trait, universe } from \'../src\';\n```\n```ts\nimport { beforeEach, describe, expect, expectTypeOf, it } from \'vitest\';\nimport { $internal, createWorld, type Entity, getStore, trait, unpackEntity } from \'../src\';\n```\n→ always import from `\'../src\'` (the barrel), inline `type` modifiers, `beforeEach` with `world.reset()` or `universe.reset()`. `tsconfig.json` extends `@config/typescript/base.json` and includes `src/**/*` + `tests`.\n\n---\n\n## Proposed public API signatures\n\nThese match the in-tree draft (`src/snapshot/snapshot.ts`) and the barrel/type wiring already present.\n\n```ts\n// ---- types ----\nexport type RelationSnapshotEntry = { targetId: number; data?: object };\n\nexport type EntitySnapshot = {\n    id: number;                                   // bare entityId (getEntityId), NOT packed\n    traits: Record<string, object | true>;        // true = tag trait\n    relations?: Record<string, RelationSnapshotEntry[]>;\n};\n\nexport type WorldSnapshot = { entities: EntitySnapshot[] };\n\nexport type EntitySnapshotDiff = {\n    addedTraits: string[];\n    removedTraits: string[];\n    changedTraits: string[];\n};\n\nexport type WorldSnapshotDiff = {\n    added: number[];\n    removed: number[];\n    changed: number[];\n};\n\nexport type TraitRegistry = {\n    readonly entries: ReadonlyMap<\n        string,\n        { key: string; trait: Trait; relation: Relation<Trait> | null }\n    >;\n    get(key: string): Trait | Relation<Trait> | undefined;\n    has(key: string): boolean;\n    keys(): string[];\n};\n\n// ---- functions ----\nexport function createTraitRegistry(\n    ...entries: Array<[string, Trait | Relation<Trait>]>\n): TraitRegistry;\n\nexport function snapshotEntity(\n    world: World,\n    entity: Entity,\n    registry: TraitRegistry\n): EntitySnapshot;\n\nexport function snapshotWorld(\n    world: World,\n    registry: TraitRegistry\n): WorldSnapshot;\n\nexport function rollbackEntity(\n    world: World,\n    entity: Entity,\n    registry: TraitRegistry,\n    snapshot: EntitySnapshot\n): void;\n\nexport function rollbackWorld(\n    world: World,\n    registry: TraitRegistry,\n    checkpoint: WorldSnapshot\n): void;\n\nexport function diffEntitySnapshots(\n    a: EntitySnapshot | null | undefined,\n    b: EntitySnapshot | null | undefined\n): EntitySnapshotDiff;\n\nexport function diffWorldSnapshots(\n    before: WorldSnapshot | null | undefined,\n    after: WorldSnapshot | null | undefined\n): WorldSnapshotDiff;\n\n// ---- convenience methods ----\n// World (src/world/types.ts:66-67)\nsnapshot(registry: TraitRegistry): WorldSnapshot;\nrollback(registry: TraitRegistry, checkpoint: WorldSnapshot): void;\n\n// Entity (src/entity/types.ts:29-30)\nsnapshot: (registry: TraitRegistry) => EntitySnapshot;\nrollback: (registry: TraitRegistry, snapshot: EntitySnapshot) => void;\n```\n\n### Behavioural contract notes (from the draft, worth preserving)\n- `createTraitRegistry` throws on: non-tuple entry, non-string key, duplicate key, duplicate trait, duplicate relation.\n- `snapshotEntity` throws if the entity is not alive, or if any trait/relation on it is not in the registry.\n- `rollbackEntity` throws if the entity is not alive; validates all registry keys **before** mutating (no partial state).\n- `rollbackWorld` validates keys *and* that every relation `targetId` exists in the checkpoint before destroying anything; then destroys all non-world entities, re-creates by id, and applies traits/relations.\n- Relations are re-added via `addTrait(world, entity, relation(target))` (pair form) so the store is created empty rather than seeded with schema defaults (`src/snapshot/snapshot.ts:346-352`).\n- `diffEntitySnapshots` compares traits only (shallow-equal per trait record); `diffWorldSnapshots` compares per-entity via `entitySnapshotsEqual` (traits + normalised, targetId-sorted relations).\n\n### Gaps to close\n1. **`tests/snapshot.test.ts` is missing** — add one following `tests/trait.test.ts` conventions (`import { createTraitRegistry, createWorld, relation, trait } from \'../src\'`).\n2. **`src/snapshot/index.ts` is missing** — decide between keeping the single `snapshot.ts` module (repo convention favours this) or adding an `index.ts` barrel; a `.js`-suffixed specifier would be the only one in the package.\n3. `rollbackWorld` re-creates entities with generation `0`; document that pre-rollback entity handles become stale.\n4. `snapshotWorld` skips `ctx.worldEntity` (the internal `IsExcluded` entity) — world-level traits are not captured.\n5. Stray scratch files `packages/core/dbg.ts` and `packages/core/scratch-snapshot.ts` are untracked and should not ship.' additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 7120, 'prompt_tokens': 55146, 'total_tokens': 62266, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 37632}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 37632, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 17514}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-flash', 'system_fingerprint': 'bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6', 'id': 'ead164a2-4d76-44ec-b4e5-a9fb257e7b7f', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None} id='lc_run--01a213e5-9641-7532-ab6a-91d928a28c64-0' tool_calls=[] invalid_tool_calls=[] usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 55146, 'output_tokens': 7120, 'total_tokens': 62266, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 37632}, 'output_token_details': {}}
