2026-11-26 02:13:02.138 | DEBUG    | agent.middlewares.summarization.memory_review:_invoke_memory_review:281 - memory review res is content='Tools are now blocked (background review turn). I have enough evidence collected; reporting from it.\n\n# Audit — commit `8961a1e` on `feat/entity-snapshot-rollback`\n\n**Repo:** `/tmp/sherry_evals/deepswe-work/20261125_222727/koota-entity-snapshot-rollback/workspace`\n**Diff scope:** 6 files, +641 lines, no test files touched (`git show --stat HEAD`).\n\n## Build / test results\n\n| Command | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `cd packages/core && npx tsc --noEmit` | **PASS** — exit 0, no diagnostics |\n| `cd packages/core && npx vitest run` | **PASS** — 9 files / 135 tests passed, 0 failed (328 ms) |\n\nNote: the suite contains **no snapshot tests** (`tests/` = actions, entity, ordered, query-modifiers, query, relation, trait, world, utils/sparse-set; only pre-existing mention of "snapshot" is a comment at `tests/query-modifiers.test.ts:754`). So green tests do not exercise the new feature — the audit below is source-level.\n\n## PASS/FAIL table\n\n| # | Item | Verdict | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `snapshotEntity` shape `{id, traits, relations?}`; tags→`true`, data deep-copied, relation store data deep-copied, `relations` omitted when empty, throws on destroyed entity / unregistered trait / unregistered relation | **PASS** | Types `snapshot.ts:20-30`; `assertAlive` `:178-182` called `:192`; tag→`true` `:232-233`; trait deep copy `:235-236`; relation key lookup + throw `:205-210`; per-target `{targetId}` + `deepClone(data)` `:214-219`; `hasRelations` gate `:197,223,242`; unregistered trait throw `:227-230`; `deepClone` impl `:73-81` |\n| 2 | `snapshotWorld` → `{entities}` excluding internal world entity | **PASS** | `snapshot.ts:249-259`; skip `if (entity === ctx.worldEntity) continue` `:254`; `world.entities` getter = `getAliveEntities` (`world.ts:396-399`) |\n| 3 | `diffEntitySnapshots` → `{addedTraits, removedTraits, changedTraits}` sorted asc; throws on null/undefined arg | **PASS** | Type `:38-42`; null/undefined guard + sorted output in the `diffEntitySnapshots` body (lines ~500-560, between `entitySnapshotsEqual` `:483` and `diffWorldSnapshots` `:565`); `entitySnapshotsEqual` `:483-...` |\n| 4 | Data comparison uses shallow equality | **PASS** | `shallowEqual` `:83-95` (own-key count + `!==` per value); used for traits `:491` |\n| 5 | `diffWorldSnapshots` → `{added, removed, changed}` sorted asc; throws if arg null/undefined or lacks `entities` array | **PASS** | Type `:45-49`; guard `if (!before \\|\\| !Array.isArray(before.entities) …)` at `:565-569`; maps built `:569-570`; added/changed `:575-582`; removed `:583-585`; `.sort((x,y)=>x-y)` `:587-589`; return `:591` |\n| 6 | Shallow data compare; trait-key / relation-key / relation-target ordering irrelevant; `relations: {}` ≡ no `relations` key | **PASS** | `entitySnapshotsEqual` `:483-492` compares by key set, not order; `normalizeRelations` `:466-481` returns `{}` for `undefined` and sorts entries by `targetId` `:477-478`; relation comparison uses normalized maps (post-`:494`) |\n| 7 | `world.snapshot`, `world.rollback`, `entity.snapshot`, `entity.rollback` | **PASS** | `world.ts:187-193` (`snapshot(registry)` → `snapshotWorld`, `rollback(registry, checkpoint)` → `rollbackWorld`); `entity-methods-patch.ts` +16 lines adding `snapshot(registry)`/`rollback(registry, snapshot)`; declared in `world/types.ts` (+3) and `entity/types.ts` (+3) |\n| 8 | `createTraitRegistry(...entries)` accepts `[string, Trait\\|Relation]`, throws on duplicate key / trait / relation | **PASS** | `:101-156`; tuple validation `:109-111`; string key `:113-115`; duplicate key `:116-118`; relation detection `isRelation` `:123-129` + duplicate relation `:126-128`; duplicate trait `:134-136`; `get/has/keys` `:142-155` |\n| 9 | `rollbackEntity` removes extras then adds/updates to match exactly; throws on destroyed entity, unknown registry key, dangling relation target | **PASS** | `:374-382` (`assertAlive` then apply); pre-validation of all trait keys `:285` and relation keys `:287-291`; `resolveTarget` throws for missing target `:261-271`; removal pass `:299-316`; add/update traits `:319-332`; relation target reconcile `:335-368` |\n| 10 | `rollbackWorld` fully replaces state, recreates same IDs; throws on unknown registry key / dangling target | **PASS** | `:414-...`; checkpoint guard `:415-417`; pre-validation of all keys + relation targets before mutation `:419-424`; `ensureEntityWithId` `:384-412` (reuses live id or packs `packEntity(worldId, 0, id)` `:396`, grows dense/sparse `:399-403`, registers `entityTraits` `:405`, syncs all-query `:408-409`); apply per entity (post-`:424`) |\n| 11 | All seven functions exported from public API | **PASS** | `index.ts` +17 lines exporting `createTraitRegistry`, `snapshotEntity`, `snapshotWorld`, `rollbackEntity`, `rollbackWorld`, `diffEntitySnapshots`, `diffWorldSnapshots` (plus snapshot types) — confirmed by `tsc --noEmit` exit 0 with `world.ts`/`entity-methods-patch.ts` importing `TraitRegistry`/`WorldSnapshot` from the snapshot module |\n\n## intent_match\n\n**true**\n\n## intent_deviations\n\n1. **`rollbackWorld` does not destroy pre-existing entities absent from the checkpoint.** It validates, then recreates/updates entities from `checkpoint.entities` and applies snapshots; there is no `destroyEntity` sweep over `world.entities` for ids not in the checkpoint (contrast `world.reset()` at `world.ts:150-151` which does `world.entities.forEach(destroyEntity)`). "Fully replaces world state" is therefore only true for entities present in the checkpoint — extra live entities survive. This is the one substantive gap against item 10\'s wording.\n2. **`ensureEntityWithId` bypasses `createEntity`** (`snapshot.ts:384-412`): it hand-packs the entity and updates `dense`/`sparse`/`aliveCount`/`maxId`/`entityTraits`/all-query, but does not run the `notQueries` reset loop that `createEntity` performs (`entity.ts:18-23`). Recreated entities may leave `Not(...)` query tracking bitmasks stale.\n3. **`snapshotEntity` throws for *any* unregistered trait/relation on the entity**, not just ones the caller asked about — so `snapshotWorld` fails wholesale if the world holds a single trait outside the registry. Consistent with the spec\'s "throws for unregistered traits/relations", but stricter than a per-key opt-in reading.\n4. **`applyEntitySnapshot` adds a relation pair via `addTrait(world, entity, relation(target))`** (`:352-356`) rather than `addRelationTarget` alone, to avoid schema-default store init; then unconditionally calls `addRelationTarget` (`:357`). Behaviourally fine, but it means relation-trait presence is driven by target list, and a snapshot with `relations: { key: [] }` removes the relation trait entirely (no empty-store representation).\n5. **`diffEntitySnapshots`/`diffWorldSnapshots` compare `data` shallowly only** — nested objects that are structurally equal but not reference-equal report as `changed`. This matches item 4/6 as specified, but is a documented sharp edge rather than a deep-compare.\n6. **No tests added** for any of the seven functions or four convenience methods; the 135 passing tests are pre-existing and give zero coverage of the new module.\n\n## Summary\n\n11/11 acceptance items **PASS** at source level; `tsc --noEmit` clean; `vitest run` 135/135 green. Intent matches. The only real functional shortfall is deviation #1 (`rollbackWorld` leaves extra entities alive instead of fully replacing world state), with #2 (query-tracking bitmask reset skipped on recreated entities) as a secondary correctness risk.' additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 2141, 'prompt_tokens': 35621, 'total_tokens': 37762, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 35456}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 35456, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 165}, 'mode