2026-11-26 02:13:16.986 | DEBUG    | agent.middlewares.summarization.memory_review:_invoke_memory_review:281 - memory review res is content='Tools are now blocked (background review turn). I have all the evidence I need from the reads and test runs already completed, so here is the full report.\n\n# Audit Report — commit `8961a1e` on `feat/entity-snapshot-rollback`\n\n**Repo:** `/tmp/sherry_evals/deepswe-work/20261125_222727/koota-entity-snapshot-rollback/workspace`\n**Commit:** `8961a1e feat(core): add entity/world snapshot and rollback system` (6 files, +641 lines, no test files touched)\n**Build/test:** `cd packages/core && npx tsc --noEmit` → **exit 0, no diagnostics**; `npx vitest run` → **9 files / 135 tests passed** (no snapshot-specific test file exists in `tests/`; `grep -rn snapshot tests/` only hits an unrelated comment at `tests/query-modifiers.test.ts:754`).\n\n## PASS/FAIL table\n\n| # | Contract item | Verdict | Evidence (file:line) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `snapshotEntity` shape `{id, traits: Record<string, object\\|true>, relations?: Record<string, Array<{targetId, data?}>>}`; tags → `true`; data traits deep-copied; relation data deep-copied when store exists; `relations` omitted when none; throws for destroyed entity / unregistered trait / unregistered relation | **PASS** | Types `snapshot.ts:20-30`; `assertAlive` `:178-182` + call `:192`; tag → `true` `:232-233`; data trait `deepClone` `:235-236`; relation key lookup + throw `:205-210`; per-target `{targetId}` `:215`; store check `:213` + `deepClone(data)` `:216-219`; unregistered trait throw `:227-230`; `relations` only attached when `hasRelations` `:241-243`; `deepClone` impl `:73-81` |\n| 2 | `snapshotWorld` → `{entities: EntitySnapshot[]}`, excludes internal world entity | **PASS** | `snapshot.ts:249-259`; skip `if (entity === ctx.worldEntity) continue` `:254`; `world.entities` getter = `getAliveEntities` (`world.ts:396-399`) |\n| 3 | `diffEntitySnapshots(a,b)` → `{addedTraits, removedTraits, changedTraits}` all sorted ascending; throws if either arg null/undefined | **PASS** | Type `snapshot.ts:38-42`; function body `:498-560` region (null/undefined guard + `addedTraits/removedTraits/changedTraits` arrays with `.sort()`); equality helper `entitySnapshotsEqual` `:483-...` |\n| 4 | Data comparison uses shallow equality | **PASS** | `shallowEqual` `snapshot.ts:83-95` (own-key count + `!==` per key, no recursion); used for trait data `:491` |\n| 5 | `diffWorldSnapshots(before, after)` → `{added, removed, changed}` sorted ascending; throws if either lacks `entities` array or is null/undefined | **PASS** | Type `snapshot.ts:45-49`; guard + maps `:560-582`; `removed` from `beforeMap` keys `:583-585`; three numeric `.sort((x,y)=>x-y)` `:587-589`; return `:591` |\n| 6 | Trait/relation data compared shallowly; trait key order, relation key order, relation target order irrelevant; `relations: {}` equals missing `relations` | **PASS** | Trait keys compared by key-set, not order `:486-492`; `normalizeRelations` returns `{}` for `undefined` and sorts entries by `targetId` `:469-481`; relation key-set comparison `:494-499`; per-entry `shallowEqual` on `data` in the `:499-560` block |\n| 7 | `world.snapshot(registry)`, `world.rollback(registry, checkpoint)`, `entity.snapshot(registry)`, `entity.rollback(registry, snapshot)` | **PASS** | `world.ts:187-193` (`snapshot` → `snapshotWorld`, `rollback` → `rollbackWorld`); `entity-methods-patch.ts` (+16 lines in commit) adds `snapshot`/`rollback` delegating to `snapshotEntity`/`rollbackEntity`; `World` type `world/types.ts` (+3), `Entity` type `entity/types.ts` (+3) |\n| 8 | `createTraitRegistry(...entries)` accepts `[string, Trait\\|Relation]`; throws on duplicate keys, duplicate traits, duplicate relations | **PASS** | `snapshot.ts:101-156`; tuple validation `:109-115`; duplicate key `:116-118`; relation detection `isRelation` `:123-129` (dup relation throw `:126-128`); dup trait throw `:134-136`; registry object `:142-155` |\n| 9 | `rollbackEntity` removes extras then adds/updates to match exactly; throws for destroyed entity, unknown registry keys, dangling relation targets | **PASS** | `rollbackEntity` `:374-382` (`assertAlive` `:380`); `applyEntitySnapshot` `:273-369`; up-front key validation `:285` (`getEntry` throws `:158-162`); relation-key-must-be-relation `:288-291`; target resolution throws `:261-271`; removal pass `:299-316`; trait add/update `:318-332`; relation target add/remove + data `:334-368` |\n| 10 | `rollbackWorld` fully replaces state, recreates entities with same IDs; throws for unknown registry keys or dangling relation targets | **PASS** | `snapshot.ts:417-467`; checkpoint guard `:418-420`; key validation `:423-431`; dangling-target validation against checkpoint ids `:433-444`; destroy-all-except-world-entity loop `:450-455`; `ensureEntityWithId` `:384-412` (reuses live id or packs `packEntity(worldId, 0, id)` `:396`, updates `dense/sparse/aliveCount/maxId` `:398-403`, registers in `entityTraits` `:405` and all-query `:407-409`); apply pass `:463-466` |\n| 11 | All seven functions exported from public API | **PASS** | `packages/core/src/index.ts` (+17 lines in commit) re-exports `createTraitRegistry`, `snapshotEntity`, `snapshotWorld`, `rollbackEntity`, `rollbackWorld`, `diffEntitySnapshots`, `diffWorldSnapshots` (plus snapshot types) from `./snapshot/snapshot`; `tsc --noEmit` clean confirms the module resolves |\n\n**All 11 items: PASS.** The 7-item acceptance checklist (items 1–7 above) is likewise all PASS.\n\n## intent_match\n**true** — the commit implements exactly the requested snapshot/rollback surface: registry, entity/world snapshot, entity/world rollback, entity/world diff, public exports, and the four convenience methods, with the specified error semantics and shallow-equality diffing.\n\n## intent_deviations\n1. **No tests added.** The commit touches only 6 source files; `packages/core/tests/` has no snapshot test file, so the new 592-line module is entirely uncovered by the suite (135 passing tests are pre-existing). Not a contract violation, but a coverage gap.\n2. **`rollbackWorld` dangling-target check is stricter than "world state".** It validates relation targets against the *checkpoint\'s* entity id set (`snapshot.ts:433-444`), not against entities that exist in the world before rollback. A checkpoint referencing an entity that exists in the world but is absent from the checkpoint throws. This matches the stated contract ("dangling relation targets" → throw) but is a design choice worth noting.\n3. **`ensureEntityWithId` bypasses `createEntity`** (`snapshot.ts:384-412`): it hand-maintains `dense`/`sparse`/`aliveCount`/`maxId`, `entityTraits`, and only the `\'\'` all-query. It does not run the `notQueries` reset loop that `createEntity` performs (`entity.ts:18-23`), so `Not(...)` query membership after a world rollback may be stale. Not covered by the contract items, but a latent behavioral difference.\n4. **Recreated entities use generation 0** (`packEntity(index.worldId, 0, id)`, `snapshot.ts:396`), so a rolled-back entity is not `===` to the pre-rollback handle if that handle had a non-zero generation. IDs match as required; identity does not.\n5. **`snapshotEntity` throws on any unregistered trait/relation present on the entity** (`:205-210`, `:227-230`) — including internal traits such as `IsExcluded` if they ever land on a non-world entity. This is per contract, but makes the registry effectively mandatory-complete for the whole world.\n6. **`setTrait(..., false)`** is used during rollback (`:331`), deliberately suppressing `Changed` events; relation data writes via `setRelationData` (`:359-365`) are not similarly suppressed. Minor asymmetry in change-tracking side effects.\n\n## Verification commands (as requested)\n- `cd packages/core && npx tsc --noEmit` → **PASS** (exit 0, no output).\n- `cd packages/core && npx vitest run` → **PASS**: `Test Files 9 passed (9)`, `Tests 135 passed (135)`, duration ~328 ms.\n\nNo files were modified.' additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 2259, 'prompt_tokens': 42150, 'total_tokens': 44409, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 41984}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 41984, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 166}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-flash', 'system_fingerprint': 'bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6', 'id': '66f08330-87fe-411c-a333-32d31783a0be', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None} id='lc_run--01a213e9-4c6b-73a3-9f0d-198363dd9735-0' tool_calls=[] invalid_tool_calls=[] usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 42150, 'output_tokens': 2259, 'total_tokens': 44409, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 41984}, 'output_token_details': {}}
