ype, _ThirdType],\n    ],\n) -> Kinded[Callable[\n    [KindN[_ValidatedLikeKind, _FirstType, _SecondType, _ThirdType]],\n    KindN[_ValidatedLikeKind, _UpdatedType, _SecondType, _ThirdType],\n]]:\n    """...docstring with doctest using Valid/Invalid..."""\n\n    @kinded\n    def factory(\n        container: KindN[_ValidatedLikeKind, _FirstType, _SecondType, _ThirdType],\n    ) -> KindN[_ValidatedLikeKind, _UpdatedType, _SecondType, _ThirdType]:\n        return container.bind_validated(function)\n\n    return factory\n```\nNote: `ValidatedLikeN` must be exported from `returns/interfaces/specific/validated.py` (it is defined there; verify the exact name/alias before use).\n\n**3. `returns/pointfree/__init__.py`** — add, alphabetically after `bind_result`:\n```python\nfrom returns.pointfree.bind_validated import bind_validated as bind_validated\n```\n(That module has no `__all__`; the package re-export list is the `__all__` equivalent.)\n\n**4. `returns/converters.py`** — add `validated_to_result`, `result_to_validated`, `validated_to_maybe`, `maybe_to_validated`, `validated_to_io`, `io_to_validated`:\n- `validated_to_result`: `Valid` → `Success`, `Invalid(errors)` → `Failure(errors)` (keeps the whole accumulated tuple).\n- `result_to_validated`: delegate to `Validated.from_result` (single error wrapped in a tuple).\n- `validated_to_maybe`: `Valid` → `Some`, `Invalid` → `Nothing`.\n- `maybe_to_validated(container, default_error)`: `Some` → `Valid`, `Nothing` → `Invalid((default_error,))`.\n- `validated_to_io`: `Valid` → `IOSuccess`, `Invalid(errors)` → `IOFailure(errors)`.\n- `io_to_validated`: `IOSuccess` → `Valid`, `IOFailure` → `Invalid((error,))`.\nImport `Validated, Valid, Invalid` from `returns.validated` and `IO, IOSuccess, IOFailure` from `returns.io` (no cycle: `converters` is a leaf module).\n\n**5. Decorator** — `validated` already exists in `returns/validated.py` (lines ~577–663) with `@validated` / `@validated(exceptions=...)` / `@validated((Exc,))` overlo