4 `class Invalid(Validated[Any, _ErrorType_co])`, and the `Valid` class following it).\n- `_entrypoint.py:51-63` registers only `Result, Validated, Maybe, IO, IOResult, Future, FutureResult, RequiresContext*` — **`Valid` and `Invalid` are absent**.\n- `strategy_from_container(Valid)` would call `Valid.from_value(...)` / `Valid.from_failure(...)`, which return `Valid`/`Invalid` respectively — so a `Valid`-typed strategy would emit `Invalid` instances, violating the type.\n\n### (3) Verification status\n\n**Not re-run.** The tool block prevented the re-run you asked for. Last known-good results from before the block:\n\n- `cond` dispatch: `Valid`/`Invalid`/`Success`/`Failure`/`Some`/`Nothing` all correct\n- `st.from_type(Validated[int, str])` → both `Valid` and `Invalid` seen\n- `check_all_laws(Validated)` → 16 passed\n- Doctests (`returns/validated.py` + `returns/methods/cond.py`) → 21 passed\n- `pytest tests/` (excluding 2 pre-existing broken collection dirs) → 648 passed, 1 xfailed, 62 subtests\n\n### What still needs to be written\n\nI have the design ready but could not apply it:\n\n1. **`containers.py`** — add `__all__ = (\'strategy_from_container\', \'validated_strategies\')` (or similar), and add a `validated_strategies` function returning `st.one_of` over `st.builds(Valid, st.from_type(value_type))` and `st.builds(Invalid, st.tuples(st.from_type(error_type)))` — note `Invalid.__init__` takes a **tuple** of errors, so it must be `st.tuples(...)`, not a bare `from_type`.\n2. **`_entrypoint.py`** — add `Valid` and `Invalid` to the imports and to `registered_types`, with a factory that dispatches to the type-specific strategy rather than the generic `from_value`/`from_failure` path.\n\n**Bottom line:** requirement (1) is satisfiable and I should have done it; requirement (2) is a genuine gap in my implementation; requirement (3) is unverified due to the tool block. Nothing here is impossible — I need a turn with write/terminal access to finish it.' additional_kwa