alid_strategy(value_type=_FirstType)` → `st.builds(Valid.from_value, st.from_type(value_type))` — uses `from_value` as required\n- `invalid_strategy(error_type=_SecondType)` → `st.builds(Invalid.from_failure, st.from_type(error_type))` — uses `from_failure`, which wraps the single error into the one-element tuple `Validated` requires\n- `validated_strategy(value_type, error_type)` → `st.one_of(valid_strategy(...), invalid_strategy(...))`\n- The `ValidatedLikeN` branch inside `strategy_from_container` retained, so `strategy_from_container(Validated)` and `st.from_type(Validated)` still work\n\n### ⚠️ One known defect in the current on-disk state\n\nThe final cleanup patch — removing the now-duplicate `_FirstType`/`_SecondType` definitions at the bottom of the file — was **rejected** ("Tool is not allowed during a background review"). The file therefore currently has the TypeVars defined **twice**: once at lines 17-18 (new) and once at the original bottom location.\n\nThis is **harmless at runtime** (the second assignment rebinds the same names to fresh TypeVars; nothing references them after that point), but it is dead code and would likely trip the project\'s `wps`/lint gate. **The fix is a 3-line deletion** of the trailing block:\n\n```python\n_FirstType = TypeVar(\'_FirstType\')\n_SecondType = TypeVar(\'_SecondType\')\n```\n\nimmediately above `def _get_type_vars(thing: type):` at the end of the file.\n\n### (3) Verification status\n\n| Check | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `cond` dispatch for `Validated`/`Result`/`Maybe` | ✅ **PASS** (run earlier): `<Valid: ok>`, `<Invalid: (\'bad\',)>`, `<Success: ok>`, `<Failure: bad>`, `<Some: ok>`, `<Nothing>` |\n| `st.from_type(Validated[int, str])` yields both `Valid` and `Invalid` | ✅ **PASS** (run earlier): `types seen: {\'Invalid\', \'Valid\'}` |\n| `st.from_type(Validated)` (bare) | ✅ **PASS** (run earlier) |\n| `strategy_from_container(Validated)(Validated[int, str])` | ✅ **PASS** (run earlier) |\n| `check_all_laws(Validated)