2026-11-26 02:28:10.212 | DEBUG    | agent.middlewares.summarization.memory_review:_invoke_memory_review:281 - memory review res is content='All tools are blocked in this background-review turn, so I\'ll report from the evidence already gathered in this session rather than retrying.\n\n## Repository state: what was already applied\n\nFrom the inspection commands that ran before the tool block, all three requested changes are **already present** in the working tree:\n\n| # | Requested change | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `bind_validated` in `returns/pointfree/__init__.py`, delegating to `Validated.bind`, exported | **Applied** | `returns/pointfree/bind_validated.py` exists and is imported/exported in `returns/pointfree/__init__.py` (grep for `bind_validated` in that file returned a hit). The factory calls `container.bind_validated(function)`, and `returns/validated.py:151` defines `bind_validated = bind` (plus aliases at lines 520 and 582), so it delegates to `Validated.bind`. |\n| 2 | `Validated` ⇄ `Result` / `Maybe` / `IO` conversions in `returns/converters.py` | **Applied** | `returns/converters.py` contains `result_to_validated`, `validated_to_result`, `validated_to_maybe`, `maybe_to_validated`, `validated_to_io`, `io_to_validated`. `IO` was added to the imports. Supporting classmethods `Validated.from_maybe` and `Validated.from_io` were added to `returns/validated.py` (alongside the pre-existing `from_result` / `from_validated`). |\n| 3 | `validated`/`safe`-style decorator returning `Valid` on success, `Invalid` on caught exceptions | **Applied** | `returns/validated.py` defines `validated` with the same overload shape as `returns/result.py`\'s `safe` (bare-decorator form, `exceptions=(...)` keyword form, and positional-tuple form), catching into `Invalid((exc,))` and returning `Valid(...)` on success. |\n\n### Semantics preserved\n- `Valid` → `Success` / `Some` / `IO(Success(...))`; `Invalid(errors)` → `Failure(errors)` / `Nothing` / `IO(Failure(errors))`.\n- Error accumulation is preserved by keeping the error **tuple** intact across conversions (`Failure(1)` → `Invalid((1,))`, and `Invalid((1, 2))` round-trips as `(1, 2)`), so accumulated errors are not flattened or lost.\n- `maybe_to_validated` takes an explicit `default_error` so `Nothing` maps to a single-element `Invalid((default_error,))`.\n\n### Circular imports\n`returns/validated.py` imports `IO` and `Maybe` at module level; `returns/converters.py` imports `Validated` lazily/at module level as the existing converters do. The import smoke test `python -c "import returns.validated, returns.converters, returns.pointfree"` succeeded, confirming no cycle.\n\n### `__all__` entries\nThe grep for `__all__` across `returns/pointfree/__init__.py`, `returns/converters.py`, `returns/validated.py`, `returns/result.py`, `returns/io.py`, `returns/maybe.py`, and `returns/__init__.py` returned **no matches** — this repo does not use `__all__` in these modules; public API is defined by plain module-level imports. So there were no `__all__` lists to update, and the new names are exported the same way as their `Result` counterparts.\n\n## Verification results (from runs completed earlier this session)\n\n- `python -m pytest -o addopts=\'\' tests/ -q --ignore=tests/test_contrib --ignore=tests/test_primitives/test_laws/test_lawful/test_laws_resolution.py` → **589 passed**.\n- `python -m pytest -o addopts=\'\' --doctest-modules returns/ -q --ignore=returns/contrib` → **291 passed** (all new docstring examples in `validated.py`, `converters.py`, and `pointfree/bind_validated.py` pass).\n- Targeted new tests `tests/test_converters/test_validated_converters.py` and `tests/test_validated/test_validated_functions/test_validated_decorator.py` → **passed**.\n- Functional smoke check confirmed: `@validated` returns `Valid(1.0)` for `f(1)` and `Invalid((ZeroDivisionError,))` for `f(0)`; all six converters round-trip correctly; `bind_validated(lambda x: Valid(x+1))(Valid(1)) == Valid(2)`.\n\n**Caveat on the two exclusions:** `tests/test_contrib` and `tests/test_primitives/test_laws/test_lawful/test_laws_resolution.py` were excluded because they fail on a pre-existing path/config issue unrelated to this change (the laws-resolution test errors during collection). I did not modify them.\n\n**Lint:** `flake8`, `mypy`, and `wemake-python-styleguide` are **not installed** in this image (`which` returned nothing), so no lint run was possible; only pytest (unit + doctest) verification was performed.\n\n## Remaining work\n\nNone of the three requested changes remain outstanding. The only unverified item is static lint/type-checking, which cannot run because the toolchain is absent from the image.' additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 1202, 'prompt_tokens': 33265, 'total_tokens': 34467, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 33024}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 33024, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 241}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-flash', 'system_fingerprint': 'bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6', 'id': '585a5391-e0bf-463f-8c47-c1ae11ebddda', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None} id='lc_run--01a213f6-fea4-77d1-95a1-2667864d914f-0' tool_calls=[] invalid_tool_calls=[] usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 33265, 'output_tokens': 1202, 'total_tokens': 34467, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 33024}, 'output_token_details': {}}
