`, `swap`, `value_or`, `unwrap` (incl. `__cause__` chaining), `failure`, equality/`equals`, do-notation (incl. short-circuit), `apply` error accumulation matrix (incl. `Invalid+Invalid` → `Invalid(('first','second'))` and function-not-called spy), `combine`, `combine_n` (incl. empty tuple), the four short-circuit laws, and law registration on the interface.\n\n**Files NOT yet created** (blocked by the read-only turn): `tests/test_pointfree.py`, `tests/test_converters/test_validated_converters.py`, `tests/test_methods/test_cond.py`, `tests/test_contrib/test_hypothesis/test_validated.py`. Draft content for `test_pointfree.py` was composed but not persisted.\n\n## Evidence gathered for the remaining files\n\n- `returns/pointfree/bind_validated.py` exists and is exported from `returns/pointfree/__init__.py`; it is `@kinded` and generic over `ValidatedLikeN`, so it also works on `Result`.\n- `returns/converters.py` exports `result_to_validated`, `validated_to_result`, `validated_to_maybe`, `validated_to_io`, `maybe_to_validated`, `io_to_validated` (doctests confirm `Failure(1) → Invalid((1,))`, `IO(Failure(1)) → Invalid((1,))`).\n- `returns/methods/cond.py` has a `ValidatedLikeN` dispatch branch (41-line diff in `5dff753f`).\n- `returns/contrib/hypothesis/containers.py` (commit `972c4400`) adds `valid_strategy`, `invalid_strategy`, `validated_strategy` and registers `ValidatedLikeN` in `strategy_from_container`; `_entrypoint.py` registers `Validated` in `registered_types`.\n- `Validated.laws()` resolves to: `ValidatedLikeN` (map/bind/apply short-circuit), `FailableN` (lash short-circuit), `ContainerN`, `ApplicativeN`, `MappableN`, `Equable`.\n- `_types_to_strategies(Validated, default_settings(Validated))` produces `one_of(builds(from_value, …), builds(from_failure, …))` for `Validated` and every interface — i.e. the strategy wiring is correct and `check_all_laws(Validated)` is viable.\n\n## Remaining work (for a write-enabled turn)\n\n1. Create `tests/test_pointfree.py` (bind_validated on Validated + Result, short-circuit, no accumulation).\n2. Create `tests/test_converters/test_validated_converters.py` (all six converters, both directions, round-trips).\n3. Create `tests/test_methods/test_cond.py` (cond dispatch to `Valid`/`Invalid` for `ValidatedLikeN`).\n4. Create `tests/test_contrib/test_hypothesis/test_validated.py` with `check_all_laws(Validated)` plus `st.from_type(Validated)` / `valid_strategy` / `invalid_strategy` / `validated_strategy` assertions.\n5. Run `python -m pytest -q -o addopts=''` (the repo's `addopts` require `pytest-cov`/`pytest-mypy-plugins`, which are absent here) and fix failures.\n\n**Caveat on `check_all_laws(Validated)`:** the `ApplicativeN` laws (`identity`, `interchange`, `homomorphism`, `composition`) are written for short-circuiting applicatives. Because `Validated.apply` *accumulates* errors, `interchange_law`/`composition_law` may legitimately fail when both sides are `Invalid` (error tuples concatenate in a different order/duplicate). If so, the correct fix is in the implementation — `returns/interfaces/specific/validated.py` should override those laws with accumulation-aware variants (as it already does for the three short-circuit laws) — not in the tests." additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 1381, 'prompt_tokens': 48180, 'total_tokens': 49561, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 48000}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 48000, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 180}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-flash', 'system_fingerprint': 'bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6', 'id': '64148f39-15e7-416f-a345-14fa00917aa6', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None} id='lc_run--01a213fc-7873-71d1-b2fb-79b7db8823f3-0' tool_calls=[] invalid_tool_calls=[] usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 48180, 'output_tokens': 1381, 'total_tokens': 49561, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 48000}, 'ou