ion, equality, pattern matching\n\n   Result: **58 passed, 3 failed** — all three failures are in my new test file, not the implementation:\n   - `test_validated_is_abstract` — `Validated(1)` is constructible (`__abstractmethods__` is empty), so the `pytest.raises(TypeError)` assertion is wrong.\n   - `test_interface_inheritance` — `issubclass(Validated, ValidatedLike2)` raises `TypeError: Subscripted generics cannot be used with class and instance checks`; must compare `ValidatedLike2.__origin__` instead.\n   - `test_unwrap_with_exception_error` — `Invalid((ValueError(...),)).unwrap()` raises `UnwrapFailedError` with `__cause__ is None`; the implementation only chains when `_inner_value` itself is an `Exception`, not when the tuple contains one.\n\n## Remaining work (not done)\n\n1. Fix those three assertions in `tests/test_validated.py`:\n   - import `inspect` and `ValidatedBasedN`; replace the abstract test with `assert inspect.isabstract(Validated)` / `assert Validated.__abstractmethods__`; replace `issubclass(..., ValidatedLike2)` with `ValidatedLike2.__origin__ is ValidatedLikeN` and add `ValidatedBased2.__origin__ is ValidatedBasedN`; drop or relax the `__cause__` assertion (assert `UnwrapFailedError` is raised and `exc_info.value.halted_container is container`).\n2. Add the remaining test files: `tests/test_pointfree.py` (`bind_validated` happy path, short-circuit on `Invalid`, kinded usage), `tests/test_converters.py` (`result_to_validated`, `validated_to_result`, `validated_to_maybe`, `validated_to_io`, `maybe_to_validated`, `io_to_validated`), `tests/test_methods/test_cond.py` (`cond` dispatch to `Valid`/`Invalid` for `ValidatedLikeN`), and `tests/test_contrib/test_hypothesis.py` (`check_all_laws(Validated)`, `st.from_type(Validated)` producing both `Valid` and `Invalid`).\n3. Re-run `python -m pytest -q -o addopts=\'\'` and confirm only the pre-existing hypothesis-repr failure remains (or fix that expectation if the task allows touching it — it\'s a test