2026-11-26 02:38:52.505 | DEBUG    | agent.middlewares.summarization.memory_review:_invoke_memory_review:281 - memory review res is content='I\'ve hit a hard blocker: the tool layer has switched this session into read-only "background review" mode, so `terminal`, `read_file`, and `patch_file` are all refused. I can\'t run pytest or edit files anymore in this turn. Here is the complete state and the exact remaining work, based on evidence gathered before the block.\n\n## What I verified\n\n**1. Plugin installation is impossible in this environment (feedback item 1 — cannot be satisfied as stated).**\n```\npip install pytest-cov pytest-mypy-plugins  →  ERROR: No matching distribution found\n  (Temporary failure in name resolution; no internet, no local wheel cache)\n```\n`pip list` shows only `pytest 9.0.3`, `pytest-subtests`, `hypothesis 6.155.2`. So `setup.cfg`\'s `addopts` (`--cov=returns ... --cov-fail-under=100 --mypy-ini-file=setup.cfg`) can never be honored here. The only way to run the suite in this container is to neutralize those flags, e.g. `python -m pytest -q -o addopts=\'\'` (or a `PYTEST_ADDOPTS` override). The coverage gate is therefore unverifiable in this sandbox — that is an environment limitation, not a code defect.\n\n**2. The `sys.path` collection error is real and reproducible (feedback item 2).**\n```\nERROR tests/test_contrib/test_hypothesis/test_laws/test_user_specified_strategy.py\nE   ModuleNotFoundError: No module named \'test_hypothesis\'\n```\nRoot cause: `tests/test_contrib/test_hypothesis/__init__.py` exists, but `tests/test_contrib/` and `tests/` have **no** `__init__.py` (verified: `find tests -name \'__init__.py\'` returns only `tests/test_contrib/test_hypothesis/__init__.py`). Under pytest\'s default `prepend` import mode the module is imported as `test_hypothesis.test_laws.test_user_specified_strategy`, so the absolute import `from test_hypothesis.test_laws import ...` only resolves when `tests/test_contrib` happens to be on `sys.