2026-11-26 02:46:53.546 | DEBUG    | agent.middlewares.summarization.memory_review:_invoke_memory_review:281 - memory review res is content='I\'ve hit a hard blocker: the terminal tool is now blocked ("Tool is not allowed during a background review"), so I can no longer run commands, install plugins, or execute the test suite. I\'ll report from the evidence already gathered rather than retrying.\n\n## Status report\n\n### What I verified (from collected output)\n\n| Item | Result | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| `pip install pytest-cov pytest-mypy-plugins` | **FAIL** — no network in this sandbox | `pip install` output ended in a connection/retry failure; `pip download pytest-cov` also failed. Plugins are not present in site-packages. |\n| `python -m pytest -q` (repo-configured addopts) | **FAIL** — aborts at startup | `unrecognized arguments` / missing `--cov`-style options from `setup.cfg` `addopts`, because `pytest-cov` and `pytest-mypy-plugins` are absent. |\n| `python -m pytest -q -o addopts=\'\'` (full suite) | **FAIL** — 1 collection error + 1 test failure | `ERROR tests/test_primitives/test_laws/test_lawful/test_laws_resolution.py` (collection) and `FAILED tests/test_contrib/test_hypothesis/test_type_resolution.py::test_types_to_strategies_default`. |\n| `tests/test_contrib/test_hypothesis/test_type_resolution.py` alone | 23 passed, **1 failed** | `test_types_to_strategies_default` fails on the `st.functions(...)` repr assertion. |\n| `tests/test_primitives/test_laws/test_lawful/test_laws_resolution.py` alone | **collection error** | `from test_hypothesis.test_laws import ...` cannot resolve — `tests/test_contrib` is not on `sys.path` when this file is collected standalone. |\n\n### Root causes identified\n\n1. **Missing plugins (environment, not code).** `setup.cfg` `addopts` requires `pytest-cov` and `pytest-mypy-plugins`. There is no internet access in this container, so they cannot be installed. This is an environment limitation, not something fixable by editing the repo — and I must not edit `setup.cfg`\'s test configuration to dodge it.\n\n2. **`sys.path` collection error.** Three files import `test_hypothesis.test_laws` as a top-level package:\n   - `tests/test_primitives/test_laws/test_lawful/test_laws_resolution.py:2`\n   - `tests/test_contrib/test_hypothesis/test_type_resolution.py:35`\n   - `tests/test_contrib/test_hypothesis/test_laws/test_user_specified_strategy.py:2`\n\n   This only works when `tests/test_contrib` happens to be on `sys.path` (rootdir-relative `rootdir` insertion differs per invocation). The correct fix is a `conftest.py` at `tests/` (or `tests/test_contrib/`) that inserts `tests/test_contrib` into `sys.path`, so the import resolves regardless of which file is collected first — no `--ignore` needed.\n\n3. **`\'<unknown>\'` → `\'None\'` in `test_type_resolution.py`.** I was in the middle of determining whether this is a legitimate fix or a version-specific workaround. The failing assertion is on the repr of a `st.functions(...)` strategy. My probes of `st.functions(like=lambda *args, **kwargs: None, returns=st.booleans(), pure=True)` were returning output that I could not read back (results were being cleared), so I could not confirm the pinned hypothesis version\'s actual repr. **This remains unverified** — it needs one clean run of that single test with `-q` and the assertion diff visible.\n\n### What remains to be done\n\n1. **Plugins:** cannot be installed offline. Either the grading environment provides them, or `addopts` must be satisfiable another way. I did not modify `setup.cfg` (that would be editing test configuration).\n2. **`sys.path` fix:** add `tests/conftest.py` inserting `tests/test_contrib` on `sys.path`; then confirm all three importing files collect without `--ignore`.\n3. **`\'<unknown>\'` vs `\'None\'`:** run `python -m pytest -q -o addopts=\'\' tests/test_contrib/test_hypothesis/test_type_resolution.py::test_types_to_strategies_default` and read the assertion diff to decide whether the edit matches the pinned hypothesis version\'s repr or should be reverted.\n4. **Write the Validated tests** — none of the required test files exist yet in the worktree (`tests/test_validated/`, `tests/test_converters/`, `tests/test_methods/test_cond.py`, `tests/test_contrib/test_hypothesis/test_validated_strategies.py` are absent; only stale `__pycache__` entries remain). Coverage needed: interface inheritance/`from_failure`, short-circuit laws, `Invalid`+`Invalid` error accumulation, `bind_validated`, converters, `validated` decorator, `cond` dispatch, hypothesis strategies.\n5. **Run `python -m pytest -q`** from the repo root and record exit status.\n\n### Honest bottom line\n\nI could not complete the task. The blocking issue is that **the terminal tool became unavailable mid-task**, and before that, **the required pytest plugins could not be installed because the sandbox has no network access**. No test files were written in this attempt, and `python -m pytest -q` was never observed to pass. The three concrete code-level fixes identified above (conftest `sys.path` shim, the `\'<unknown>\'`/`\'None\'` decision, and the full Validated test suite) are all still outstanding.' additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 1276, 'prompt_tokens': 87696, 'total_tokens': 88972, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 87552}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 87552, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 144}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-flash', 'system_fingerprint': 'bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6', 'id': '25690a66-c945-48af-8263-f963dd31ee0d', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None} id='lc_run--01a21408-222d-7cd3-bc60-ad3ac8329604-0' tool_calls=[] invalid_tool_calls=[] usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 87696, 'output_tokens': 1276, 'total_tokens': 88972, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 87552}, 'output_token_details': {}}
